- What do you think, kid? Chinese?

467
00:28:07,144 --> 00:28:09,355
No way. This is nothing like
what the Chinese are using.

468
00:28:12,942 --> 00:28:14,861
This is Air Force One.
Level of flight, level three-three-zero.

469
00:28:14,944 --> 00:28:17,029
<i>We will hunt down this enemy.
And when we do,</i>

470
00:28:17,113 --> 00:28:19,323
<i>we'll know just what to do with them.</i>

471
00:28:19,782 --> 00:28:22,034
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

472
00:28:38,801 --> 00:28:40,428
<i>Apparently, there are
very few survivors.</i>

473
00:28:40,511 --> 00:28:41,721
Yes, Mr. President?

474
00:28:41,804 --> 00:28:44,807
Yeah, can you wrangle me up
some Ding Dongs, darling?

475
00:28:56,903 --> 00:29:00,990
I joined the Air Force to bring the man
Ding Dongs. I'll be in storage.

476
00:29:26,349 --> 00:29:27,350
Shoot.

477
00:29:41,489 --> 00:29:43,032
Gross.

478
00:30:10,226 --> 00:30:11,894
Do you hear that?

479
00:30:14,855 --> 00:30:16,440
Are you getting this?

480
00:30:17,400 --> 00:30:19,068
I think they're hacking
the network again.

481
00:30:34,250 --> 00:30:37,420
Oh, my God. This is a direct match
to the signal in Qatar.

482
00:30:37,503 --> 00:30:39,338
- Are you running a diagnostic?
- Should I be?

483
00:30:39,422 --> 00:30:41,465
- Yes, you should.
- So I am.

484
00:30:52,601 --> 00:30:54,854
Someone!
They're hacking into Air Force One!

485
00:30:54,937 --> 00:30:56,522
We need a senior analyst.

486
00:30:56,605 --> 00:30:58,482
- I think they're planting a virus.
- A virus?

487
00:30:58,566 --> 00:31:01,110
- It's streaming right now.
- They are planting a virus

488
00:31:01,193 --> 00:31:04,405
and stealing a whole lot of data
from your system at the same time.

489
00:31:04,488 --> 00:31:06,032
Code Red. We have a breach.

490
00:31:06,115 --> 00:31:08,868
Air Force One, someone on board
has breached the military network.

491
00:31:08,951 --> 00:31:11,787
I'm in the cargo hold. Clear. Clear.

492
00:31:16,333 --> 00:31:17,752
- You got to cut the hard lines.
- What?

493
00:31:17,835 --> 00:31:21,005
- Whatever they want, they are getting it.
- Sir?

494
00:31:21,088 --> 00:31:23,799
Permission to take down
the Defence Network.

495
00:31:23,883 --> 00:31:27,928
- Cut all server hard lines now.
- Cut all server hard lines now.

496
00:31:49,533 --> 00:31:52,328
Someone's tampered
with the POTUS mainframe.

497
00:31:52,453 --> 00:31:53,913
What the...

498
00:31:59,335 --> 00:32:01,754
<i>Shots fired in the underdeck.
Repeat, shots fired.</i>

499
00:32:01,837 --> 00:32:04,715
<i>Crew, prepare for emergency descent.</i>

500
00:32:22,775 --> 00:32:24,777
I want our President in that bunker.

501
00:32:24,860 --> 00:32:28,948
And I don't want to discuss a damn
thing other till that becomes reality.

502
00:32:29,031 --> 00:32:32,118
That's our first priority.
That's our only priority right now.

503
00:32:32,201 --> 00:32:33,369
Air Force One is on the ground.

504
00:33:37,433 --> 00:33:40,102
Oh, God. No, no, no, no, no, no, no!

505
00:33:40,936 --> 00:33:42,521
That's my car!

506
00:33:43,939 --> 00:33:45,274
No!

507
00:33:47,401 --> 00:33:48,527
No, no, no, no.

508
00:33:56,035 --> 00:33:58,162
Dad, call the cops!

509
00:33:59,914 --> 00:34:03,042
Where you going with my car, buddy?
Where you going?

510
00:34:03,125 --> 00:34:06,879
Hello? 911 emergency!
My car has been stolen!

511
00:34:06,962 --> 00:34:10,466
I'm in pursuit! Right?
I need all units, the whole squadron.

512
00:34:10,549 --> 00:34:13,385
Bring everyone!
No, don't ask me questions, all right?

513
00:34:13,469 --> 00:34:16,138
My father's the head
of the neighbourhood watch!

514
00:34:48,754 --> 00:34:50,339
Oh, my God.

515
00:35:06,730 --> 00:35:08,148
My name is Sam Witwicky.

516
00:35:08,232 --> 00:35:12,194
Whoever finds this, my car is alive,
okay? You saw that?

517
00:35:12,278 --> 00:35:15,030
Since this is my last words on Earth,
I just wanna say, Mom, Dad, I love you,

518
00:35:15,114 --> 00:35:17,491
and if you find <i>Busty Beauties</i>
under my bed, it wasn't mine.

519
00:35:17,574 --> 00:35:19,618
I'm holding it for Miles.
No, no, wait that...

520
00:35:19,702 --> 00:35:22,329
Okay, that's not true. It's mine
and Uncle Charles gave it to me.

521
00:35:22,413 --> 00:35:24,415
I'm sorry. Mojo, I love you.

522
00:35:36,051 --> 00:35:38,220
No! No! No! No!

523
00:35:41,724 --> 00:35:43,142
Oh, my God.

524
00:35:43,684 --> 00:35:46,228
No, you're a good dog!
Good dog! Good dog!

525
00:35:46,395 --> 00:35:47,563
Oh, my God.

526
00:35:50,816 --> 00:35:55,571
Whoa! Hey, hey, hey! All right! Oh!
No! No!

527
00:35:58,407 --> 00:35:59,825
Okay. Please, please don't kill me!

528
00:35:59,908 --> 00:36:03,245
I'm sorry! Take the keys!
I don't want them! Car's yours!

529
00:36:05,039 --> 00:36:07,499
Listen, listen, listen.

530
00:36:07,583 --> 00:36:08,917
- Good, you're here.
- Let me see your hands!

531
00:36:09,001 --> 00:36:10,586
- No, no, no! It's not me!
- Let me see your hands.

532
00:36:10,669 --> 00:36:13,756
- The guy's inside.
- Shut up! Walk towards the car.

533
00:36:15,674 --> 00:36:17,426
Put your head on the hood.

534
00:36:30,689 --> 00:36:33,442
Whoever did this finally managed
to infiltrate our defence network,

535
00:36:33,525 --> 00:36:36,070
which is what they tried to do in Qatar,
only this time it worked.

536
00:36:36,153 --> 00:36:37,821
- What did they get?
- We still don't know.

537
00:36:37,905 --> 00:36:41,033
- Talk to me about the virus.
- It's a Spider-bot virus.

538
00:36:41,116 --> 00:36:43,786
We're not sure what it's going to do,
but it may cripple the system.

539
00:36:43,869 --> 00:36:45,871
- Can we stop it?
- Every time we try an antivirus,

540
00:36:45,954 --> 00:36:48,540
it adapts and speeds up.
It's like it's not a virus any more.

541
00:36:48,624 --> 00:36:49,708
It's become the system.

542
00:36:49,792 --> 00:36:52,961
Obviously the first phase
of a major attack against the US.

543
00:36:53,045 --> 00:36:54,671
The only countries
with this kind of capability

544
00:36:54,755 --> 00:36:57,049
are Russia, North Korea, maybe China.

545
00:36:57,132 --> 00:37:00,094
- I'm sorry, that's not correct.
- Excuse me, young lady.

546
00:37:00,177 --> 00:37:02,429
I didn't see you standing there.
You would be who?

547
00:37:02,513 --> 00:37:04,390
I'm just the analyst
who detected the hack.

548
00:37:04,473 --> 00:37:07,643
Hold on. It was you? You did it?

549
00:37:07,976 --> 00:37:10,729
- Her team.
- Sir, I was just trying to say,

550
00:37:10,813 --> 00:37:13,482
they hacked your firewall in 10 seconds.

551
00:37:13,565 --> 00:37:16,235
Okay. Even a supercomputer
with a brute force attack

552
00:37:16,318 --> 00:37:18,070
would take 20 years to do that.

553
00:37:18,153 --> 00:37:20,656
Maybe you can explain, then,
how our latest satellite imagery

554
00:37:20,739 --> 00:37:23,075
shows North Korea
doubling its naval activity.

555
00:37:23,158 --> 00:37:26,703
Maybe it's a precaution,
because isn't that what we're doing?

556
00:37:26,787 --> 00:37:30,165
The signal pattern is learning.
It's evolving on its own.

557
00:37:30,249 --> 00:37:32,543
And you need to
move past Fourier transfers

558
00:37:32,626 --> 00:37:34,837
and start considering
quantum mechanics.

559
00:37:34,920 --> 00:37:37,256
There is nothing on Earth that complex.

560
00:37:37,339 --> 00:37:39,883
What about an organism?
A living organism?

561
00:37:39,967 --> 00:37:42,386
Maybe some kind of
DNA-based computer?

562
00:37:42,469 --> 00:37:46,181
- And I know that that sounds crazy...
- That's enough. That's enough.

563
00:37:46,598 --> 00:37:49,184
We have six floors of analysts
working on this thing.

564
00:37:49,268 --> 00:37:51,603
Now, if you can find proof to back up
your theory,

565
00:37:51,687 --> 00:37:54,231
I'm gonna be happy to listen to you.
But if you don't get a filter

566
00:37:54,314 --> 00:37:58,277
on that brain-mouth thing, you're gonna
be off the team. You understand?

567
00:38:03,699 --> 00:38:07,202
Look, I can't be any clearer
than how crystal clear I am being.

568
00:38:08,036 --> 00:38:10,456
- It just stood up.
- It just stood up.

569
00:38:11,915 --> 00:38:13,709
Wow. That's really neat.

570
00:38:14,668 --> 00:38:15,919
Okay, chiefie.

571
00:38:16,295 --> 00:38:19,089
Time to fill her up. And no drippy-drippy.

572
00:38:19,590 --> 00:38:20,966
What are you rolling?

573
00:38:21,049 --> 00:38:23,427
Whippets? Goofballs?
A little wowie sauce with the boys?

574
00:38:23,510 --> 00:38:25,888
- No, I'm not on any drugs.
- What's these?

575
00:38:26,680 --> 00:38:29,516
Found it in your pocket. "Mojo."

576
00:38:30,726 --> 00:38:33,353
Is that what the kids are doing now?
Little bit of Mojo?

577
00:38:33,437 --> 00:38:37,107
- Those are my dog's pain pills.
- You know, a Chihuahua. A little...

578
00:38:41,069 --> 00:38:42,362
What was that?

579
00:38:43,989 --> 00:38:47,201
You eyeballing my piece, 50 Cent?

580
00:38:48,327 --> 00:38:51,830
You wanna go?
Make something happen. Do it.

581
00:38:51,914 --> 00:38:55,125
'Cause I promise you I will bust you up.

582
00:38:56,335 --> 00:38:57,628
Are you on drugs?

583
00:39:06,303 --> 00:39:08,597
Let's hope this telephone line works.

584
00:39:11,099 --> 00:39:13,560
Hey, heads up!

585
00:39:13,644 --> 00:39:17,314
Heads up! Hey! Heads up!

586
00:39:22,236 --> 00:39:24,238
What the heck was that?

587
00:39:28,867 --> 00:39:31,245
English, dude. English.

588
00:39:37,626 --> 00:39:38,794
Whoa!

589
00:39:39,419 --> 00:39:40,963
Watch out!

590
00:39:47,177 --> 00:39:49,680
- Open fire!
- Contact! Contact!

591
00:39:49,763 --> 00:39:50,847
Everybody, quiet. Settle.

592
00:39:50,931 --> 00:39:53,100
Whoa, mother... What the hell is...

593
00:40:00,816 --> 00:40:03,610
Get up! Get up! Come on!

594
00:40:10,659 --> 00:40:12,494
Go! Move it!

595
00:40:24,756 --> 00:40:26,925
Take cover!

596
00:40:29,261 --> 00:40:31,305
Fig! Cover the rear!

597
00:40:31,888 --> 00:40:36,810
Cover fire! Move it! Fig, cover the rear!
Epps! Cover the rear! Move it!

598
00:40:36,893 --> 00:40:39,980
Come on! Give me a mag!

599
00:40:41,189 --> 00:40:42,774
Where's your papa?
Where's your papa?

600
00:40:42,858 --> 00:40:44,026
Papa!

601
00:40:44,610 --> 00:40:46,862
Sir, we need... I need a telephone.

602
00:40:46,945 --> 00:40:49,323
- Telephone, telephone, yes!
- Telephone!

603
00:40:49,406 --> 00:40:51,033
Hey, I need a mag! Give me a mag!

604
00:40:51,116 --> 00:40:52,409
- Cell phone!
- I don't know how to thank you.

605
00:40:52,492 --> 00:40:53,493
Fire!

606
00:40:54,703 --> 00:40:57,289
This is an emergency Pentagon call!
I need you to... Do you understand?

607
00:40:57,372 --> 00:40:59,875
It's an emergency Pentagon...

608
00:41:01,710 --> 00:41:03,879
I don't have a credit card!

609
00:41:04,338 --> 00:41:08,091
Sir, the attitude is not going to speed
things up any bit at all.

610
00:41:08,175 --> 00:41:10,886
I'm going to ask you to speak
into the mouthpiece very clearly.

611
00:41:10,969 --> 00:41:15,307
I'm in the middle of a war!
This is frigging ridiculous!

612
00:41:16,600 --> 00:41:17,934
Ammo!

613
00:41:18,435 --> 00:41:20,687
I need a credit card!

614
00:41:22,606 --> 00:41:25,400
- Epps! Where's your wallet?
- Pocket!

615
00:41:26,068 --> 00:41:28,779
- Which pocket?
- My back pocket!

616
00:41:28,862 --> 00:41:33,075
- You got 10 back pockets!
- Left cheek! Left cheek! Left cheek!

617
00:41:33,909 --> 00:41:36,078
All right, keep shooting! Keep shooting!

618
00:41:36,161 --> 00:41:38,205
Okay, it's Visa.

619
00:41:38,413 --> 00:41:39,665
Also, sir, have you heard about

620
00:41:39,748 --> 00:41:41,875
our premium plus
world-service gold package?

621
00:41:41,958 --> 00:41:47,130
No, I don't want a premium package!
Epps! Pentagon!

622
00:41:50,092 --> 00:41:51,426
Give me a status.

623
00:41:51,760 --> 00:41:54,346
Sir, we're tracking a Special Ops team
under fire in Qatar.

624
00:41:54,429 --> 00:41:56,181
They say they're survivors
of the base attack.

625
00:41:56,264 --> 00:41:57,265
Survivors?

626
00:42:01,061 --> 00:42:02,729
I ain't never seen this in my life!

627
00:42:02,813 --> 00:42:04,564
<i>Need gunships on station ASAP!</i>

628
00:42:04,648 --> 00:42:05,857
Predator's coming up in a minute.

629
00:42:05,941 --> 00:42:07,401
We're linking the call
to the nearest AWACS.

630
00:42:13,615 --> 00:42:16,618
Unknown, man. I don't...
Man, if you seen this shit...

631
00:42:16,952 --> 00:42:19,621
Predator ETA two minutes.

632
00:42:28,338 --> 00:42:30,298
Hey! Make way!

633
00:42:35,137 --> 00:42:37,264
- What is that?
- I don't know.

634
00:42:42,477 --> 00:42:44,229
We need air support
and we need it now.

635
00:42:44,312 --> 00:42:47,399
Roll in strike package Bravo
on unknown target.

636
00:42:47,482 --> 00:42:51,111
<i>I authenticate Tango Whiskey
at time 0300 Zulu.</i>

637
00:42:51,194 --> 00:42:54,072
<i>Attention, all aircraft. This will be
a danger close-fire mission.</i>

638
00:42:54,156 --> 00:42:55,699
<i>Weapons, I just got a call
from Falcon Ops.</i>

639
00:42:55,782 --> 00:42:57,492
<i>Who's closer to Kill Box One Alpha?</i>

640
00:42:57,576 --> 00:42:59,119
- Send the Hogs, sir.
<i>- Okay, send the Hogs over</i>

641
00:42:59,202 --> 00:43:00,912
<i>to Kill Box One Alpha.
It's a danger close...</i>

642
00:43:00,996 --> 00:43:03,582
<i>Switch the Hogs to Kill Box One Alpha,
300 feet danger close.</i>

643
00:43:03,665 --> 00:43:05,584
<i>Friendlies in the area.</i>

644
00:43:05,667 --> 00:43:08,712
Seven-man team
north of orange smoke!

645
00:43:08,795 --> 00:43:12,048
Received Kill Box One Alpha.
Engage hostile.

646
00:43:14,384 --> 00:43:17,679
Attack direction west!
You're clear and hot!

647
00:43:20,849 --> 00:43:22,267
<i>Strike, tell me status of Hog right now.</i>

648
00:43:22,350 --> 00:43:24,227
Hog One-One Dark Star status.

649
00:43:26,563 --> 00:43:29,691
- Lennox! The heat's coming!
- Laze the target!

650
00:43:29,775 --> 00:43:32,360
We got a beam-rider incoming!
Laze target!

651
00:43:39,701 --> 00:43:42,329
- Ready! Heat's coming!
- What? Bring it!

652
00:43:42,412 --> 00:43:45,040
<i>Receiving radar jamming
in vicinity of target.</i>

653
00:44:01,389 --> 00:44:03,183
No frigging way
that thing's still not down.

654
00:44:03,266 --> 00:44:06,561
Spooky Three Two, use 105 shells.
Bring the rain.

655
00:44:08,730 --> 00:44:12,234
<i>Be advised, ground team is requesting
105 sabot rounds.</i>

656
00:44:40,428 --> 00:44:41,513
Did we lose them?

657
00:44:41,596 --> 00:44:44,224
<i>Warthog One confirm visual
on friendlies.</i>

658
00:44:48,270 --> 00:44:49,437
Where's Fig?

659
00:44:50,355 --> 00:44:51,982
- Fig? Fig?
- Oh, God!

660
00:44:52,941 --> 00:44:54,734
- God damn it!
- Get a medic!

661
00:44:54,818 --> 00:44:55,944
Get a medic!

662
00:44:56,111 --> 00:44:57,153
- I'm sorry.
- Black Hawk...

663
00:44:57,237 --> 00:44:58,446
We'll get a medic. Just hold on.
He's got a pulse.

664
00:44:58,530 --> 00:45:00,448
We need a medevac. One man down.
Patient care category urgent.

665
00:45:06,121 --> 00:45:07,873
Bring them home.

666
00:45:09,249 --> 00:45:11,626
<i>You get those men stateside right now.</i>

667
00:45:11,960 --> 00:45:13,670
<i>I want them debriefed in 10 hours.</i>

668
00:45:20,552 --> 00:45:23,972
There's only one hacker in the world
who can break this code.

669
00:45:34,399 --> 00:45:37,152
Hey! Hey, hey, hey! Wait! Stop!

670
00:45:40,196 --> 00:45:41,948
I am sorry to bother you.

671
00:45:42,198 --> 00:45:43,867
- Maggie?
- Listen, I need your help.

672
00:45:43,950 --> 00:45:47,954
No! This is my private area,
my place of Zen and peace.

673
00:45:48,038 --> 00:45:49,748
- Listen to me.
- Glen! Who is it?

674
00:45:49,831 --> 00:45:51,958
Shut up, Grandma!

675
00:45:52,042 --> 00:45:54,502
- What are you doing here?
- Just give me a break, will you, please?

676
00:45:54,586 --> 00:45:56,713
Grandmama! Drink your prune juice!

677
00:46:01,676 --> 00:46:04,220
- What level are you on, man?
- Six.

678
00:46:07,015 --> 00:46:09,726
Oh, here come the matrix!
Here come the matrix!

679
00:46:13,313 --> 00:46:16,149
Glen, seriously, don't you
want to see something classified?

680
00:46:16,232 --> 00:46:18,109
Yeah. Get low.

681
00:46:18,401 --> 00:46:22,364
- Here we go. Here we go. Double tap.
- Hey, I just paused it. I just paused it.

682
00:46:22,447 --> 00:46:24,324
Hey. I need a moment.

683
00:46:25,283 --> 00:46:26,660
- Please.
- Sorry.

684
00:46:27,202 --> 00:46:28,787
Hey, man, save my game.

685
00:46:28,870 --> 00:46:30,789
How classified?

686
00:46:32,082 --> 00:46:36,211
Like "I will go to jail for the rest of
my life for showing you" classified.

687
00:46:36,419 --> 00:46:38,421
Yes! One quick peek.

688
00:46:39,214 --> 00:46:42,384
Special Ops got a thermal snapshot
of whatever hit the base in Qatar.

689
00:46:42,467 --> 00:46:45,011
- I want to see it.
- Well, the imager was damaged, sir.

690
00:46:45,095 --> 00:46:46,680
The rangers are en route
with the imager,

691
00:46:46,763 --> 00:46:48,682
but we also have a security issue.

692
00:46:48,765 --> 00:46:51,059
Circle logs indicate one of
the analysts made a copy

693
00:46:51,142 --> 00:46:52,852
of the network intrusion signal.

694
00:46:55,814 --> 00:46:59,150
The signal strength is through the roof.
Where did you say you got this?

695
00:46:59,234 --> 00:47:01,569
It hacked the national military
air-guard frequency

696
00:47:01,653 --> 00:47:03,238
in less than a minute.

697
00:47:03,321 --> 00:47:05,573
- No way.
- Yeah.

698
00:47:06,992 --> 00:47:11,454
Looks like there's a message embedded
in the signal. Let me work my magic.

699
00:47:17,585 --> 00:47:19,170
"Project Iceman"?

700
00:47:19,254 --> 00:47:22,674
- What's Sector Seven?
- Who is Captain Witwicky?

701
00:47:24,175 --> 00:47:26,553
Are you playing
those video games again?

702
00:47:26,720 --> 00:47:28,722
Cops! Cops!

703
00:47:28,805 --> 00:47:31,558
FBI! Clear right!

704
00:47:33,268 --> 00:47:35,478
Lock it down! Lock it down!

705
00:47:37,147 --> 00:47:38,148
Cops!

706
00:47:38,398 --> 00:47:39,566
Lock it down.

707
00:47:39,649 --> 00:47:43,194
Wait! I'm just a cousin! I'm just a...

708
00:47:44,279 --> 00:47:47,866
Get off my Grandmama's carpet!
She don't like nobody on the carpet!

709
00:47:47,949 --> 00:47:49,617
Especially police!

710
00:47:50,160 --> 00:47:52,954
<i>It was an awesome spectacle here
an hour ago</i>

711
00:47:53,038 --> 00:47:56,958
<i>when over 40 C-17s lifted off
of this very base.</i>

712
00:47:57,542 --> 00:47:59,586
<i>We're not told where they're going.</i>

713
00:47:59,669 --> 00:48:00,712
Morning, Mo.

714
00:48:00,795 --> 00:48:03,089
<i>The government has been very quiet
about what's going on but in our...</i>

715
00:48:03,173 --> 00:48:04,841
- Mojo. Mojo.
<i>- They were headed directly</i>

716
00:48:04,924 --> 00:48:06,468
<i>towards North Korea.</i>

717
00:48:06,551 --> 00:48:09,471
Stop with the barking, Mojo.
It's too early. Please?

718
00:48:13,016 --> 00:48:14,809
Miles? Miles, listen to me. Listen.

719
00:48:14,893 --> 00:48:17,937
- My car, it stole itself, okay?
- What are you talking about, man?

720
00:48:18,021 --> 00:48:20,982
Satan's Camaro. In my yard.
It's stalking me.

721
00:48:28,823 --> 00:48:29,866
Stop!

722
00:48:29,949 --> 00:48:31,701
No, no, no, no, no, no.

723
00:48:38,166 --> 00:48:39,334
Oh, my God!

724
00:48:40,168 --> 00:48:41,169
Sam?

725
00:48:44,214 --> 00:48:45,215
Hi.

726
00:48:45,507 --> 00:48:48,760
That was... That was really awesome.

727
00:48:48,843 --> 00:48:50,970
- Well, it felt awesome.
- Are you okay?

728
00:48:51,054 --> 00:48:53,098
I'm not okay, all right?
I'm losing my mind a little bit.

729
00:48:53,181 --> 00:48:55,058
I'm getting chased by my car right now.
I got to go.

730
00:48:55,141 --> 00:48:57,393
You know what?
I'm gonna catch up with you guys later.

731
00:49:30,260 --> 00:49:31,886
Oh, great. Cops.

732
00:49:36,933 --> 00:49:38,184
Officer!

733
00:49:39,769 --> 00:49:41,563
Listen!

734
00:49:43,064 --> 00:49:44,065
Oh, that hurt.

735
00:49:46,776 --> 00:49:48,319
Listen to me!

736
00:49:48,403 --> 00:49:51,281
Thank God you're here!
I've had the worst day ever!

737
00:49:51,364 --> 00:49:55,034
I've been... I've been followed here
on my mother's bike! Right?

738
00:49:55,118 --> 00:49:57,745
And my car's right there
and it's been following me here!

739
00:49:57,829 --> 00:50:04,335
So get out of the car! No! Stop!
Oh, God. Okay, okay! Okay, all right!

740
00:50:04,627 --> 00:50:09,132
Okay! I'm sorry! I'm...
I didn't mean to hit your car! Look!

741
00:50:10,425 --> 00:50:14,304
Okay, look, look, look! Stop, stop!

742
00:50:18,433 --> 00:50:21,269
Please! Okay,
what do you want from me?

743
00:50:23,563 --> 00:50:24,981
Okay.

744
00:50:30,486 --> 00:50:31,988
Oh, God, no! No!

745
00:50:33,907 --> 00:50:39,370
Oh, shit! Oh, shit, shit, shit!
Oh, God! Oh, shit!

746
00:50:42,373 --> 00:50:44,167
It's a bad dream.

747
00:50:46,002 --> 00:50:47,795
Are you username LadiesMan21 7?

748
00:50:47,879 --> 00:50:49,047
I don't know what you're talking about!

749
00:50:49,130 --> 00:50:51,549
Are you username LadiesMan21 7?

750
00:50:51,633 --> 00:50:52,759
Yeah.

751
00:50:52,842 --> 00:50:55,303
Where is eBay item 21153?

752
00:50:55,386 --> 00:50:57,138
Where are the glasses?

753
00:51:08,650 --> 00:51:09,984
Get back!

754
00:51:10,818 --> 00:51:11,819
Stop!

755
00:51:14,948 --> 00:51:15,949
God!

756
00:51:16,824 --> 00:51:18,576
What is your problem, Sam?

757
00:51:18,660 --> 00:51:20,703
Okay, there's a monster right there!
It just attacked me!

758
00:51:20,787 --> 00:51:25,250
Here he comes! All right, get up.
Get up and run! You have to run! Okay.

759
00:51:32,882 --> 00:51:33,925
Sam, what is that thing?

760
00:51:34,008 --> 00:51:35,426
- You have to get in the car. Get in.
- I don't want to.

761
00:51:35,510 --> 00:51:37,595
- Get in the car. Trust me. Trust me!
- Sam.

762
00:51:37,679 --> 00:51:42,100
Get in! Go, go, go, go, go.

763
00:51:53,695 --> 00:51:55,029
Go, go, go, go!

764
00:51:59,617 --> 00:52:01,452
Oh, God! We're gonna die!
We're gonna die!

765
00:52:01,536 --> 00:52:03,121
No, we're not. No, we're not gonna die.

766
00:52:03,204 --> 00:52:05,540
- Oh, my God!
- Trust me. He's a kick-ass driver!

767
00:52:06,124 --> 00:52:07,542
Oh, my God! No!

768
00:52:07,625 --> 00:52:08,960
We're gonna die!

769
00:52:14,966 --> 00:52:16,384
Oh, my God!

770
00:52:33,735 --> 00:52:34,902
We're locked in.

771
00:52:37,405 --> 00:52:40,867
The car won't start.
At least we ditched the monster, right?

772
00:52:46,748 --> 00:52:47,874
Okay.

773
00:52:49,417 --> 00:52:50,918
Time to start.

774
00:53:55,233 --> 00:53:56,567
He's got me! Oh, God!

775
00:54:03,074 --> 00:54:04,992
He's going to kill me!

776
00:54:08,079 --> 00:54:09,789
No. No, no, no!

777
00:54:24,345 --> 00:54:25,555
Get off!

778
00:54:40,194 --> 00:54:41,237
Kill it! Kill it!

779
00:54:41,320 --> 00:54:42,905
Get it, get it, get it, get it!

780
00:54:49,704 --> 00:54:51,706
Not so tough without a head, are you?

781
00:54:57,628 --> 00:54:59,088
Here, come on.

782
00:55:13,895 --> 00:55:15,396
What is it?

783
00:55:16,772 --> 00:55:18,232
It's a robot.

784
00:55:19,609 --> 00:55:20,943
But like a...

785
00:55:21,068 --> 00:55:24,572
Like a different...
You know, like a super-advanced robot.

786
00:55:25,907 --> 00:55:27,366
It's probably Japanese.

787
00:55:27,450 --> 00:55:29,911
Yeah, it's definitely Japanese.

788
00:55:31,454 --> 00:55:33,206
What are you doing?

789
00:55:33,789 --> 00:55:37,001
I don't think it wants to hurt us.
It would have done that already.

790
00:55:37,084 --> 00:55:39,378
Really? Well, do you speak robot?

791
00:55:39,462 --> 00:55:42,924
Because they just had, like,
a giant droid death match.

792
00:55:44,258 --> 00:55:47,428
- I think it wants something from me.
- What?

793
00:55:47,512 --> 00:55:50,056
Well, 'cause the other one was
talking about my eBay page.

794
00:55:50,890 --> 00:55:53,684
You are the strangest boy
I have ever met.

795
00:55:54,143 --> 00:55:56,354
- Can you talk?
- <i>XM Satellite Radio...</i>

796
00:55:56,437 --> 00:56:00,024
<i>Digital cable brings you...</i>
...<i>Columbia Broadcasting System...</i>

797
00:56:00,107 --> 00:56:01,859
So you... You talk through the radio?

798
00:56:01,943 --> 00:56:04,862
<i>Thank you, you're beautiful.
You're wonderful, you're wonderful.</i>

799
00:56:04,946 --> 00:56:06,989
So, what was that last night?
What was that?

800
00:56:07,073 --> 00:56:08,533
<i>Message from Starfleet, Captain...</i>

801
00:56:08,616 --> 00:56:10,701
<i>Throughout the inanimate vastness
of space...</i>

802
00:56:10,785 --> 00:56:12,787
<i>Angels will rain down
like visitors from heaven! Hallelujah!</i>

803
00:56:12,870 --> 00:56:15,039
Visitors from heaven? What...

804
00:56:15,122 --> 00:56:17,291
What are you,
like, an alien or something?

805
00:56:23,047 --> 00:56:25,591
<i>Any more questions you want to ask?</i>

806
00:56:26,217 --> 00:56:28,427
He wants us to get in the car.

807
00:56:29,428 --> 00:56:30,930
And go where?

808
00:56:31,889 --> 00:56:33,683
Fifty years from now,
when you're looking back at your life,

809
00:56:33,808 --> 00:56:36,894
don't you want to be able to say
you had the guts to get in the car?

810
00:57:06,340 --> 00:57:08,092
This car's a pretty good driver.

811
00:57:08,175 --> 00:57:09,343
I know.

812
00:57:12,013 --> 00:57:14,015
Why don't you go sit in that seat, there?

813
00:57:14,098 --> 00:57:16,267
I'm not going to sit in that seat.
He's driving.

814
00:57:16,350 --> 00:57:17,476
Yeah.

815
00:57:18,853 --> 00:57:20,354
You're right.

816
00:57:21,856 --> 00:57:24,859
- Well, maybe you should sit in my lap.
- Why?

817
00:57:26,027 --> 00:57:29,822
Well, I have the only seat belt here.
You know, safety first.

818
00:57:31,866 --> 00:57:33,284
- Yeah, all right.
- Right?

819
00:57:33,367 --> 00:57:34,952
- Yeah.
- Okay.

820
00:57:37,371 --> 00:57:39,415
There, see? That's better.

821
00:57:39,707 --> 00:57:41,125
- Okay.
- Okay.

822
00:57:44,795 --> 00:57:48,215
You know, that seat belt thing was
a pretty smooth move.

823
00:57:49,216 --> 00:57:50,217
Thank you.

824
00:57:51,260 --> 00:57:53,429
You know what I don't understand?

825
00:57:53,512 --> 00:57:56,599
Why, if he's supposed to be, like,
this super-advanced robot,

826
00:57:56,682 --> 00:57:59,310
does he transform back
into this piece-of-crap Camaro?

827
00:58:00,728 --> 00:58:02,021
Whoa! Whoa!

828
00:58:02,104 --> 00:58:04,899
Oh, see? No. Get...
No, that doesn't work. See?

829
00:58:04,982 --> 00:58:06,067
Move it, you moron!

830
00:58:06,150 --> 00:58:08,235
Great, now... See?

831
00:58:09,570 --> 00:58:10,738
Fantastic.

832
00:58:10,821 --> 00:58:12,740
Now you pissed him off.

833
00:58:12,990 --> 00:58:14,492
That car is sensitive.

834
00:58:14,575 --> 00:58:16,786
I mean, $4000 just drove off.

835
00:58:29,924 --> 00:58:31,050
What?

836
00:59:34,780 --> 00:59:36,157
This is you...

837
00:59:41,287 --> 00:59:43,205
Oh, my God!

838
00:59:50,421 --> 00:59:52,173
Come on, let's go.

839
00:59:57,011 --> 01:00:00,264
This is the coolest thing I've ever seen!
Explosions everywhere!

840
01:00:00,347 --> 01:00:03,851
This is easily a hundred times cooler
than <i>Armageddon.</i> I swear to God!

841
01:00:03,934 --> 01:00:06,187
Fire, fire, fire, fire!

842
01:00:20,117 --> 01:00:21,786
Whoa! Sweet!

843
01:00:21,869 --> 01:00:23,996
Oh, dude, I hope this guy's got
asteroid insurance,

844
01:00:24,079 --> 01:00:25,372
'cause he is so boned!

845
01:00:29,251 --> 01:00:30,628
What is that?

846
01:00:31,128 --> 01:00:32,755
There's something in the tree, dude.

847
01:00:32,838 --> 01:00:34,965
No, there's something
in the thing by the tree!

848
01:00:35,049 --> 01:00:36,425
Could you guys just give me
a space rock?

849
01:01:11,794 --> 01:01:14,338
Excuse me, are you the tooth fairy?

850
01:01:15,589 --> 01:01:18,926
Hey, sweetheart, what are you doing
out here by yourself?

851
01:01:19,009 --> 01:01:21,554
Holy God! What happened to the pool?

852
01:02:54,021 --> 01:02:58,275
Are you Samuel James Witwicky,
descendent of Archibald Witwicky?

853
01:02:59,401 --> 01:03:01,195
They know your name.

854
01:03:02,112 --> 01:03:03,113
Yeah.

855
01:03:03,197 --> 01:03:05,616
My name is Optimus Prime.

856
01:03:05,699 --> 01:03:09,787
We are autonomous robotic organisms
from the planet Cybertron.

857
01:03:09,870 --> 01:03:13,290
- But you can call us Autobots for short.
- Autobots.

858
01:03:13,457 --> 01:03:18,754
- What's cracking, little bitches?
- My first lieutenant. Designation, Jazz.

859
01:03:18,837 --> 01:03:22,383
This looks like a cool place to kick it.

860
01:03:22,925 --> 01:03:24,802
What is that?
How did he learn to talk like that?

861
01:03:24,885 --> 01:03:28,555
We've learned Earth's languages
through the World Wide Web.

862
01:03:30,015 --> 01:03:32,518
My weapons specialist, Ironhide.

863
01:03:33,394 --> 01:03:36,981
- You feeling lucky, punk?
- Easy, Ironhide.

864
01:03:37,064 --> 01:03:40,317
Just kidding.
I just wanted to show him my cannons.

865
01:03:41,527 --> 01:03:43,696
Our medical officer, Ratchet.

866
01:03:43,779 --> 01:03:47,950
The boy's pheromone level suggests
he wants to mate with the female.

867
01:03:50,327 --> 01:03:53,706
You already know
your guardian, Bumblebee.

868
01:03:53,914 --> 01:03:55,582
Bumblebee, right?

869
01:03:55,666 --> 01:03:57,376
<i>Check on the rep
Yep, second to none</i>

870
01:03:57,459 --> 01:03:59,837
So you're my guardian, huh?

871
01:03:59,920 --> 01:04:05,175
His vocal processors were damaged
in battle. I'm still working on them.

872
01:04:09,972 --> 01:04:11,348
Why are you here?

873
01:04:11,432 --> 01:04:16,729
We are here looking for the All Spark.
And we must find it before Megatron.

874
01:04:17,021 --> 01:04:18,480
Mega-what?

875
01:04:28,032 --> 01:04:33,662
<i>Our planet was once a powerful empire,
peaceful and just,</i>

876
01:04:34,705 --> 01:04:39,585
<i>until we were betrayed by Megatron,
leader of the Decepticons.</i>

877
01:04:40,627 --> 01:04:43,922
<i>All who defied them were destroyed.</i>

878
01:04:44,006 --> 01:04:50,137
<i>Our war finally consumed the planet,
and the All Spark was lost to the stars.</i>

879
01:04:51,096 --> 01:04:57,144
<i>Megatron followed it to Earth,
where Captain Witwicky found him.</i>

880
01:04:58,270 --> 01:04:59,980
My grandfather.

881
01:05:00,064 --> 01:05:04,318
<i>It was an accident
that intertwined our fates.</i>

882
01:05:07,488 --> 01:05:09,073
Come back!

883
01:05:11,575 --> 01:05:14,161
I think the dogs have found something.

884
01:05:15,204 --> 01:05:16,997
The ice is cracking!

885
01:05:26,340 --> 01:05:29,426
Captain! Grab my rope, Captain!

886
01:05:30,135 --> 01:05:32,179
I'm all right, lads!

887
01:05:33,305 --> 01:05:35,974
Can we throw you a rope, Captain?

888
01:05:43,315 --> 01:05:48,445
<i>Megatron crash-landed
before he could retrieve the Cube.</i>

889
01:05:51,990 --> 01:05:55,452
Men! We've made a discovery!

890
01:05:55,536 --> 01:05:59,998
<i>He accidentally activated
his navigation system.</i>

891
01:06:13,554 --> 01:06:19,393
<i>The coordinates to the Cube's location
on Earth were imprinted on his glasses.</i>

892
01:06:19,476 --> 01:06:21,520
How'd you know about his glasses?

893
01:06:21,603 --> 01:06:23,856
- EBay.
- eBay.

894
01:06:23,939 --> 01:06:27,151
If the Decepticons find the All Spark,

895
01:06:27,234 --> 01:06:33,073
they will use its power to transform
Earth's machines and build a new army.

896
01:06:33,157 --> 01:06:36,577
And the human race
will be extinguished.

897
01:06:36,660 --> 01:06:42,166
Sam Witwicky,
you hold the key to Earth's survival.

898
01:06:45,127 --> 01:06:48,130
Please tell me
that you have those glasses.

899
01:06:52,259 --> 01:06:55,679
It's like
a self-regenerating molecular armour.

900
01:06:55,762 --> 01:06:57,806
Look at the scorch mark
where the sabot round hit.

901
01:06:57,890 --> 01:06:59,183
Melted right through.

902
01:06:59,266 --> 01:07:02,477
Hey, aren't sabots hot-loaded for, like,
a 6,000-degree magnesium burn?

903
01:07:02,603 --> 01:07:04,813
Close to it. It melts tank armour.

904
01:07:04,897 --> 01:07:07,107
So this metal skin must react
to extreme heat.

905
01:07:07,441 --> 01:07:09,526
- Heads up!
- Oh!

906
01:07:10,235 --> 01:07:12,946
I thought you said
that thing was dead, man!

907
01:07:13,280 --> 01:07:17,034
Strap it down! Strap it!
This thing is wicked.

908
01:07:17,117 --> 01:07:18,493
All right, get on the horn
with Northern Command.

909
01:07:18,577 --> 01:07:20,871
Tell them that our effective weapon
is high-heat sabot rounds.

910
01:07:20,954 --> 01:07:22,456
Recommend we load them
on all the gunships. Go.

911
01:07:27,628 --> 01:07:29,379
You want that piece?

912
01:07:29,463 --> 01:07:32,758
Okay, Maggie, look. Let me break
it down to you how it's gonna happen.

913
01:07:32,841 --> 01:07:34,927
They gonna come through that door
and be good cop, bad cop.

914
01:07:35,010 --> 01:07:38,388
Don't fall for that, all right?
That's why I ate their food.

915
01:07:38,472 --> 01:07:41,058
See, they put the plate of donuts
out here to test your guilt.

916
01:07:41,141 --> 01:07:43,602
If you don't touch it, you're guilty.

917
01:07:43,685 --> 01:07:47,564
I ate the whole plate.
The whole plate. Okay?

918
01:07:47,648 --> 01:07:48,815
It's me and you.

919
01:07:48,899 --> 01:07:51,777
They walk through that door,
you don't say nothing.

920
01:08:05,791 --> 01:08:08,835
She did it! She did it!
She's the one you want! All right?

921
01:08:08,919 --> 01:08:10,587
I was just sitting at home
watching cartoons,

922
01:08:10,671 --> 01:08:12,673
playing video games with my cousin,
and she came in there.

923
01:08:12,756 --> 01:08:13,757
- And then...
- Glen, you freak.

924
01:08:13,840 --> 01:08:16,093
Hey! I am not going to jail for you
or anybody else!

925
01:08:16,176 --> 01:08:20,889
I have done nothing bad my entire life!
Hey, man, I'm still a virgin.

926
01:08:20,973 --> 01:08:21,932
Okay, so what?

927
01:08:22,015 --> 01:08:24,142
I've downloaded a couple of
thousand songs off the Internet.

928
01:08:24,226 --> 01:08:25,936
Who hasn't? Who hasn't?

929
01:08:26,019 --> 01:08:27,020
- I promise!
- Glen, shut up!

930
01:08:27,104 --> 01:08:30,983
No, you shut up! Don't talk to me!
Don't talk to me, criminal!

931
01:08:33,235 --> 01:08:35,362
- Oh, sugar rush.
- This is... This is not his fault.

932
01:08:35,445 --> 01:08:37,072
See? So can I go home now?

933
01:08:37,155 --> 01:08:39,408
- Oh, okay. I won't.
- But just listen to me.

934
01:08:39,491 --> 01:08:43,203
Okay, whoever hacked into your military
system downloaded a file, all right?

935
01:08:43,287 --> 01:08:45,622
It was something about
someone named Witwicky

936
01:08:45,706 --> 01:08:49,334
and some government group, right?
Named Sector Seven.

937
01:08:49,418 --> 01:08:51,169
You have to let me talk to
Defence Secretary Keller

938
01:08:51,253 --> 01:08:53,588
before you go to war
with the wrong country!

939
