01:18:08,351 --> 01:18:09,686
I'm carrying a loaded weapon.

1161
01:18:09,769 --> 01:18:11,145
But you'd better get those guys
out of my garden

1162
01:18:11,229 --> 01:18:13,398
or I am gonna beat the crap out of them!

1163
01:18:13,481 --> 01:18:16,526
Are you experiencing any flu-like
symptoms? Aching joints? Fever?

1164
01:18:16,609 --> 01:18:18,695
- No!
- What is this?

1165
01:18:18,778 --> 01:18:21,531
How you doing, son?
Is your name Sam?

1166
01:18:21,614 --> 01:18:23,116
- Yeah.
- Well, I need you to come with us.

1167
01:18:23,199 --> 01:18:24,450
Whoa, way out of line.

1168
01:18:24,534 --> 01:18:28,580
Sir, I am asking politely. Back off.

1169
01:18:28,663 --> 01:18:30,582
- You're not taking my son.
- Really?

1170
01:18:30,665 --> 01:18:31,749
You gonna try to get rough with us?

1171
01:18:31,833 --> 01:18:33,042
No, but I'm gonna call the cops

1172
01:18:33,126 --> 01:18:35,378
because there's something fishy
going on around here.

1173
01:18:35,461 --> 01:18:38,172
Yeah. There's something a little fishy
about you, your son,

1174
01:18:38,256 --> 01:18:42,218
your little Taco Bell dog and this
whole operation you got going on here.

1175
01:18:42,302 --> 01:18:44,554
- What operation?
- That is what we are gonna find out.

1176
01:18:44,637 --> 01:18:47,265
I think direct contact.

1177
01:18:52,645 --> 01:18:54,272
- Son?
- Yeah.

1178
01:18:55,315 --> 01:18:58,234
- Step forward, please.
- Just stand?

1179
01:19:03,990 --> 01:19:05,491
Fourteen rads.

1180
01:19:07,035 --> 01:19:08,536
Bingo! Tag them and bag them!

1181
01:19:09,245 --> 01:19:11,164
If you hurt my dog, I'll kick your ass!

1182
01:19:11,247 --> 01:19:12,957
Get me a sample on
that vegetation ASAP!

1183
01:19:13,041 --> 01:19:14,584
Sam! Do not say anything, Sam!

1184
01:19:14,667 --> 01:19:16,586
- Yeah.
- Not a word until we get a lawyer!

1185
01:19:20,840 --> 01:19:22,008
So,

1186
01:19:23,426 --> 01:19:26,930
LadiesMan21 7.

1187
01:19:27,013 --> 01:19:30,433
That is your eBay username, right?

1188
01:19:30,516 --> 01:19:32,894
Yeah, but, you know,
it was a typo and I ran with it.

1189
01:19:32,977 --> 01:19:33,937
What do you make of this?

1190
01:19:34,020 --> 01:19:36,606
<i>My name is Sam Witwicky, okay?
And my...</i>

1191
01:19:36,689 --> 01:19:37,857
Is that you?

1192
01:19:37,941 --> 01:19:40,151
Yeah, that sounds like Ladies Man.

1193
01:19:40,234 --> 01:19:45,114
Last night at the station, you told
the officer your car transformed.

1194
01:19:46,407 --> 01:19:48,785
- Enlighten me.
- Well, here's what I said, okay?

1195
01:19:48,868 --> 01:19:53,331
'Cause this is a total misunderstanding
that my car had been stolen...

1196
01:19:53,414 --> 01:19:55,583
- Really?
- ...from me, from my home,

1197
01:19:55,667 --> 01:19:58,628
but it's fine now because it's back!
It came back!

1198
01:19:58,711 --> 01:20:00,463
- Well, not by itself.
- Well, no.

1199
01:20:00,546 --> 01:20:04,050
Because cars don't do that
because that would be crazy.

1200
01:20:07,136 --> 01:20:08,763
That's funny. That is so funny.

1201
01:20:08,846 --> 01:20:11,391
So what do you kids know
about aliens, huh?

1202
01:20:12,517 --> 01:20:15,311
Oh, you mean, like a Martian?
Like what, <i>E. T.?</i> No.

1203
01:20:15,395 --> 01:20:16,896
- It's an urban legend.
- Yeah.

1204
01:20:16,980 --> 01:20:18,147
You see this?

1205
01:20:18,231 --> 01:20:20,817
This is an I-can-do-whatever-I-want
and-get-away-with-it badge.

1206
01:20:20,900 --> 01:20:23,695
- Right.
- I'm gonna lock you up forever.

1207
01:20:23,778 --> 01:20:25,029
Oh, God. You know what?
Don't listen to him.

1208
01:20:25,113 --> 01:20:27,532
He's just pissy 'cause he's got to
get back to guarding the mall.

1209
01:20:27,615 --> 01:20:30,702
You, in the training bra, do not test me.

1210
01:20:30,785 --> 01:20:32,912
Especially with your daddy's parole
coming up.

1211
01:20:32,996 --> 01:20:34,414
What? Parole?

1212
01:20:34,497 --> 01:20:37,834
- It's nothing.
- Oh, grand theft auto, that ain't nothing?

1213
01:20:37,917 --> 01:20:39,961
You know those cars my dad
used to teach me to fix?

1214
01:20:40,044 --> 01:20:41,796
Well, they... They weren't always his.

1215
01:20:41,879 --> 01:20:43,006
You stole cars?

1216
01:20:43,089 --> 01:20:44,799
Well, we couldn't always afford
a babysitter,

1217
01:20:44,882 --> 01:20:46,676
so sometimes he had to take me along.

1218
01:20:46,759 --> 01:20:49,095
She's got her own juvie record
to prove it!

1219
01:20:49,178 --> 01:20:51,848
She's a criminal. Criminals are hot.

1220
01:20:52,932 --> 01:20:57,603
That'd be a real shame if he had to rot
in jail the rest of his natural life.

1221
01:20:57,687 --> 01:21:00,023
It is time to talk!

1222
01:21:06,738 --> 01:21:08,197
Big! It's big!

1223
01:21:12,910 --> 01:21:14,912
Go, go, go, go!

1224
01:21:15,288 --> 01:21:17,957
- I can't see it! I can't see it!
- Shift your weight towards the front!

1225
01:21:18,041 --> 01:21:19,500
All right! All right!

1226
01:21:34,057 --> 01:21:36,392
You A-holes are in trouble now.

1227
01:21:36,476 --> 01:21:43,024
Gentlemen, I want to introduce you
to my friend, Optimus Prime.

1228
01:21:45,234 --> 01:21:49,030
Taking the children was a bad move.

1229
01:21:49,113 --> 01:21:52,533
Autobots, relieve them of their weapons.

1230
01:21:56,120 --> 01:21:57,872
Freeze!

1231
01:21:58,498 --> 01:21:59,916
- Whoa! Whoa!
- Give me those!

1232
01:21:59,999 --> 01:22:01,084
Whoa!

1233
01:22:02,502 --> 01:22:03,586
Whoa!

1234
01:22:14,347 --> 01:22:15,681
Hi, there.

1235
01:22:15,973 --> 01:22:20,728
You don't seem afraid.
Are you not surprised to see us?

1236
01:22:21,395 --> 01:22:26,359
Look, there are
S-Seven protocols, okay?

1237
01:22:26,943 --> 01:22:28,277
I'm not authorised
to communicate with you

1238
01:22:28,361 --> 01:22:30,613
except to tell you
I can't communicate with you.

1239
01:22:30,696 --> 01:22:33,324
- Get out of the car.
- All right.

1240
01:22:33,908 --> 01:22:35,076
- Me? You want me to get...
- Now!

1241
01:22:35,159 --> 01:22:36,661
All right, all right. Get out. Hey.

1242
01:22:36,744 --> 01:22:40,123
All right, I'm... I'm getting out.
I'm getting out. You see?

1243
01:22:40,206 --> 01:22:43,751
Very nifty how you put us down
without really killing us.

1244
01:22:43,835 --> 01:22:45,378
You're good with handcuffs, too,
now, huh?

1245
01:22:45,461 --> 01:22:46,462
How you doing?

1246
01:22:46,546 --> 01:22:48,297
- You weren't supposed to hear all that.
- How's it going, huh?

1247
01:22:48,381 --> 01:22:50,591
- Yeah.
- This is real.

1248
01:22:50,675 --> 01:22:53,845
Now, listen. If I choose to engage
with him, mum is the word, all right?

1249
01:22:53,928 --> 01:22:57,723
Sam, I have a record
because I wouldn't turn my dad in.

1250
01:22:58,307 --> 01:23:02,520
When have you had to sacrifice
anything in your perfect little life?

1251
01:23:04,063 --> 01:23:05,731
Big guys. Big guys with big guns, huh?

1252
01:23:05,815 --> 01:23:08,693
What is Sector Seven? Answer me.

1253
01:23:08,776 --> 01:23:11,320
I'm the one who asks questions
around here. Not you, young man!

1254
01:23:11,404 --> 01:23:13,656
- How'd you know about the aliens?
- Where did you take my parents?

1255
01:23:13,739 --> 01:23:15,741
- I am not at liberty to discuss it.
- No?

1256
01:23:15,825 --> 01:23:17,702
Hey. You touch me,
that's a federal offence.

1257
01:23:17,785 --> 01:23:19,537
Do-whatever-you-want
and-get-away-with-it badge, right?

1258
01:23:19,620 --> 01:23:22,498
Yeah. Brave now all of a sudden, with
his big alien friend standing over there.

1259
01:23:22,582 --> 01:23:25,793
- Where is Sector Seven?
- Wouldn't you like to know?

1260
01:23:31,048 --> 01:23:32,008
Hey!

1261
01:23:32,091 --> 01:23:35,052
Bumblebee, stop lubricating the man.

1262
01:23:35,136 --> 01:23:37,096
Get that thing to stop, huh?

1263
01:23:38,556 --> 01:23:41,851
- All right, tough guy, take it off.
- What are you talking about?

1264
01:23:41,934 --> 01:23:44,687
- Your clothes, all of it, off.
- For what?

1265
01:23:45,897 --> 01:23:47,773
For threatening my dad.

1266
01:23:50,776 --> 01:23:56,741
Little lady, this is the beginning
of the end of your life.

1267
01:23:58,451 --> 01:24:00,161
You're a criminal.

1268
01:24:00,786 --> 01:24:03,623
Let's face facts. It's in your gene pool.

1269
01:24:05,082 --> 01:24:07,919
Those are nice.
Now get behind the pole.

1270
01:24:08,002 --> 01:24:09,045
All right.

1271
01:24:09,128 --> 01:24:11,255
This is such a felony, what you're doing.

1272
01:24:13,257 --> 01:24:15,176
- I will hunt you down, okay?
- He'll hunt you down.

1273
01:24:15,301 --> 01:24:17,470
- Without any remorse!
- No remorse.

1274
01:24:17,553 --> 01:24:18,846
- Enjoy.
- Okay?

1275
01:24:18,930 --> 01:24:23,392
- We have got to alert everyone.
- They already know. Speaker.

1276
01:24:29,899 --> 01:24:31,859
Optimus! Incoming!

1277
01:24:39,533 --> 01:24:40,826
Roll out.

1278
01:24:47,667 --> 01:24:51,045
<i>Okay, I'm picking up rad readings
under that bridge right down there.</i>

1279
01:24:53,881 --> 01:24:57,301
<i>Okay, I'm getting really good rad
readings. Forty-two and higher.</i>

1280
01:24:57,385 --> 01:24:58,761
Up you get.

1281
01:25:03,432 --> 01:25:05,434
<i>Okay, we're dropping in.</i>

1282
01:25:09,438 --> 01:25:12,066
<i>Really strong readings right down
below us. There he is.</i>

1283
01:25:12,149 --> 01:25:14,360
<i>Ship one and two, come on in.</i>

1284
01:25:15,361 --> 01:25:18,030
<i>That's it, right there.
Mark him, mark him.</i>

1285
01:25:18,114 --> 01:25:21,409
<i>Okay, there he is. 11:30. 11:30.
Right off the nose.</i>

1286
01:25:21,909 --> 01:25:23,536
<i>I got it. 12:00.</i>

1287
01:25:27,540 --> 01:25:29,041
<i>Okay, I'm tracking him. I've got him.</i>

1288
01:25:31,961 --> 01:25:34,213
<i>Got him going down the street.</i>

1289
01:25:37,758 --> 01:25:42,388
<i>Okay. Where'd he go, guys? I lost him.
Got no IR signature. Where'd he go?</i>

1290
01:25:42,680 --> 01:25:44,890
<i>Okay, I lost him. I lost him.</i>

1291
01:25:45,391 --> 01:25:47,435
<i>Okay, we're coming around.</i>

1292
01:26:10,082 --> 01:26:11,667
Easy, you two.

1293
01:26:21,010 --> 01:26:24,263
No! No! No, Sam! Sam, don't drop me!

1294
01:26:24,930 --> 01:26:27,933
Sam, don't! Sam, don't! I'm slipping!
I'm slipping!

1295
01:26:29,143 --> 01:26:31,270
- Hold on!
- No!

1296
01:26:34,940 --> 01:26:36,192
Sam!

1297
01:26:41,781 --> 01:26:44,909
<i>All right, we've got him pinned.
We've got him pinned in the river.</i>

1298
01:26:44,992 --> 01:26:46,285
<i>I'm in for the shot.</i>

1299
01:26:46,369 --> 01:26:47,828
Stop! Stop!

1300
01:26:48,996 --> 01:26:50,831
Wait! No!

1301
01:26:54,168 --> 01:26:56,796
<i>- Take the shot, get him.
- Take the shot.</i>

1302
01:26:57,338 --> 01:26:58,589
No!

1303
01:27:14,647 --> 01:27:16,774
No! Stop!

1304
01:27:17,316 --> 01:27:18,651
Stop!

1305
01:27:19,235 --> 01:27:22,696
<i>Get down on the ground! Get down!
Get down!</i>

1306
01:27:23,656 --> 01:27:25,032
What? Okay.

1307
01:27:26,867 --> 01:27:29,078
Look, he's not fighting back!

1308
01:27:29,662 --> 01:27:31,872
Freeze it! Freeze it! Freeze it!

1309
01:27:38,212 --> 01:27:39,839
Stop hurting him!

1310
01:27:49,181 --> 01:27:50,933
Don't let him move!

1311
01:27:51,642 --> 01:27:53,227
I got him here!

1312
01:28:16,375 --> 01:28:17,501
No!

1313
01:28:21,464 --> 01:28:23,299
Happy to see me again?

1314
01:28:24,758 --> 01:28:27,553
Put him in a car
with his little criminal friend.

1315
01:28:33,392 --> 01:28:36,479
I want that thing frozen
and ready for transport!

1316
01:28:44,612 --> 01:28:46,906
Hang back. Let me check it out.

1317
01:28:49,742 --> 01:28:51,160
Optimus,

1318
01:28:53,454 --> 01:28:55,956
are we just gonna stand here
and do nothing?

1319
01:28:56,040 --> 01:28:59,752
There's no way to free Bumblebee
without harming the humans.

1320
01:28:59,835 --> 01:29:02,671
- But it's not right. He...
- Let them leave.

1321
01:29:14,642 --> 01:29:17,019
The Chinese and the Russians
are nearing our area of operations

1322
01:29:17,102 --> 01:29:18,270
in the western Pacific.

1323
01:29:18,354 --> 01:29:20,564
We feel like this could get
out of hand real fast.

1324
01:29:20,648 --> 01:29:23,442
But the next couple of hours
may just define his presidency.

1325
01:29:27,780 --> 01:29:30,658
US and Chinese task forces
approaching 100 nautical miles

1326
01:29:30,741 --> 01:29:32,076
of cruise missile range.

1327
01:29:32,159 --> 01:29:35,704
Tell the strike group commander that
he's not to engage unless fired on first.

1328
01:29:35,788 --> 01:29:37,790
- Yes, sir!
- Mr. Secretary?

1329
01:29:40,167 --> 01:29:45,256
Tom Banachek. I'm with Sector Seven,
Advanced Research Division.

1330
01:29:45,339 --> 01:29:48,592
Never heard of it. I'm a little busy, Tom.
I think you can see that.

1331
01:29:51,679 --> 01:29:54,223
- What's going on here?
- I don't know.

1332
01:29:57,810 --> 01:30:00,521
Sit rep! Talk to me!

1333
01:30:00,604 --> 01:30:03,023
- The whole room's gone down, sir.
- I can see that!

1334
01:30:03,107 --> 01:30:04,775
The virus was coded to shut us down.

1335
01:30:04,858 --> 01:30:07,319
- General?
- I'll take a seat.

1336
01:30:08,320 --> 01:30:09,321
What do you mean, "shut us down"?

1337
01:30:09,405 --> 01:30:12,408
They used our network to spread out
to the whole world.

1338
01:30:12,491 --> 01:30:13,617
The blackout's global.

1339
01:30:13,701 --> 01:30:16,579
We have no communications,
satellite and land lines are dead.

1340
01:30:16,662 --> 01:30:21,208
You mean to tell me that I cannot pick
up this telephone and call my family?

1341
01:30:27,131 --> 01:30:31,468
Mr. Secretary? I'm here under
direct order from the President.

1342
01:30:33,429 --> 01:30:35,848
You really need to see
what I have in the case.

1343
01:30:38,851 --> 01:30:40,436
You'll have to accept that
there are certain things

1344
01:30:40,519 --> 01:30:42,646
you won't understand right away.

1345
01:30:42,730 --> 01:30:46,108
Sector Seven is a special-access
division of the government

1346
01:30:46,191 --> 01:30:49,612
convened in secret under
President Hoover 80 years ago.

1347
01:30:50,446 --> 01:30:54,575
You may remember NASA JPL
lost the Beagle 2 Mars Rover.

1348
01:30:55,659 --> 01:30:59,955
We told them to report the mission
a complete failure. It wasn't.

1349
01:31:00,372 --> 01:31:02,833
Beagle 2 transmitted 13 seconds.

1350
01:31:03,375 --> 01:31:05,961
This was classified above top secret.

1351
01:31:20,893 --> 01:31:23,520
<i>EDA ended at 170 hours, 48 minutes.</i>

1352
01:31:23,604 --> 01:31:26,273
More than just a pile of Martian rocks.

1353
01:31:27,524 --> 01:31:29,652
This is the image from Mars.

1354
01:31:30,444 --> 01:31:33,238
Here's the image your
Special Ops team was able to retrieve

1355
01:31:33,322 --> 01:31:35,115
from the base attack.

1356
01:31:35,866 --> 01:31:38,994
We believe they are of
the same exoskeletal type,

1357
01:31:39,828 --> 01:31:42,623
and obviously not Russian
or North Korean.

1358
01:31:42,998 --> 01:31:45,668
Are we talking about an invasion?

1359
01:31:45,751 --> 01:31:48,879
We intercepted the message
from your Special Ops team.

1360
01:31:48,962 --> 01:31:52,341
These things can be hurt by
our weapons and now they know it.

1361
01:31:52,424 --> 01:31:54,176
That's why the virus shut us down,

1362
01:31:54,259 --> 01:31:57,554
so we can't coordinate against
their next attack,

1363
01:31:57,638 --> 01:32:02,184
which I would bet my ridiculous
government salary is coming soon.

1364
01:32:06,021 --> 01:32:08,357
Get word to our fleet commanders
over the National Guard frequency.

1365
01:32:08,440 --> 01:32:11,860
It's a shortwave radio channel.
It might be still working.

1366
01:32:11,944 --> 01:32:15,322
Tell them to turn their ships around
and come home. ASAP!

1367
01:32:15,406 --> 01:32:18,409
And inform all commands to prepare
for imminent attack.

1368
01:32:28,585 --> 01:32:31,880
Captain Lennox, we need you and
your team to come with us right now!

1369
01:32:31,964 --> 01:32:32,965
Let's go!

1370
01:32:37,970 --> 01:32:39,471
She's in here.

1371
01:32:39,805 --> 01:32:41,515
What's going on?

1372
01:32:42,015 --> 01:32:43,892
You're coming with me.

1373
01:32:44,309 --> 01:32:47,020
- You're going to be my advisor.
- Me, too?

1374
01:32:47,980 --> 01:32:49,356
Who's this?

1375
01:32:50,107 --> 01:32:53,235
- He's my advisor.
- He comes, too.

1376
01:33:04,496 --> 01:33:06,999
- So...
- What'd they get you for?

1377
01:33:08,041 --> 01:33:12,337
I bought a car.
Turned out to be an alien robot.

1378
01:33:12,421 --> 01:33:13,422
Wow.

1379
01:33:14,047 --> 01:33:15,215
Who knew?

1380
01:33:31,982 --> 01:33:33,901
Make a hole! Watch your back!

1381
01:33:44,703 --> 01:33:47,456
Please, let this work.

1382
01:33:48,832 --> 01:33:50,751
Fire it up, Optimus.

1383
01:33:51,710 --> 01:33:53,212
The code.

1384
01:33:53,295 --> 01:33:58,717
The code on these glasses indicates
the All Spark is 230 miles from here.

1385
01:34:00,511 --> 01:34:04,348
I sense the Decepticons
are getting ready to mobilise.

1386
01:34:05,474 --> 01:34:07,267
They must know it's here, as well.

1387
01:34:07,351 --> 01:34:08,685
What about Bumblebee?

1388
01:34:08,769 --> 01:34:12,856
We can't just leave him to die
and become some human experiment!

1389
01:34:12,940 --> 01:34:16,985
He'll die in vain
if we don't accomplish our mission.

1390
01:34:17,069 --> 01:34:21,323
Bumblebee is a brave soldier.
This is what he would want.

1391
01:34:21,406 --> 01:34:24,368
Why are we fighting to save
the humans?

1392
01:34:25,744 --> 01:34:29,122
<i>They're a primitive and violent race.</i>

1393
01:34:31,416 --> 01:34:33,460
Were we so different?

1394
01:34:34,336 --> 01:34:38,715
<i>They're a young species.
They have much to learn.</i>

1395
01:34:38,799 --> 01:34:41,635
<i>But I've seen goodness in them.</i>

1396
01:34:41,718 --> 01:34:45,889
<i>Freedom is the right of
all sentient beings.</i>

1397
01:34:45,973 --> 01:34:50,227
<i>You all know there's only one way
to end this war.</i>

1398
01:34:50,310 --> 01:34:53,063
<i>We must destroy the Cube.</i>

1399
01:34:53,814 --> 01:34:58,402
If all else fails, I will unite it
with the spark in my chest.

1400
01:34:58,485 --> 01:34:59,862
That's suicide.

1401
01:34:59,945 --> 01:35:03,740
The Cube is raw power.
It could destroy you both.

1402
01:35:03,824 --> 01:35:08,328
A necessary sacrifice to bring peace
to this planet.

1403
01:35:08,412 --> 01:35:11,748
We cannot let the humans pay
for our mistakes.

1404
01:35:13,166 --> 01:35:15,878
It's been an honour serving with you all.

1405
01:35:15,961 --> 01:35:19,798
- Autobots, roll out!
- We rolling!

1406
01:35:31,810 --> 01:35:35,022
Team attention! Present arms!

1407
01:35:35,647 --> 01:35:39,902
At ease. Captain, Sergeant.
Got your intel. Excellent work.

1408
01:35:39,985 --> 01:35:41,737
Thank you, sir.
What about the gunships?

1409
01:35:41,820 --> 01:35:43,947
They're being retrofitted
with sabot rounds now.

1410
01:35:44,031 --> 01:35:45,324
If they hit us again,
we'll be ready for them.

1411
01:35:45,407 --> 01:35:48,535
But it won't do us much good if we can't
get world communications back up.

1412
01:35:49,995 --> 01:35:51,288
Hey, kid.

1413
01:35:52,331 --> 01:35:55,000
I think we got off to a bad start, huh?

1414
01:35:55,500 --> 01:35:56,627
You must be hungry?

1415
01:35:56,710 --> 01:35:58,754
You want a latte? HoHo?
Double venti macchiato?

1416
01:35:58,837 --> 01:36:00,464
Where's my car?

1417
01:36:00,547 --> 01:36:04,176
Son, I need you to listen to me
very carefully.

1418
01:36:04,635 --> 01:36:06,345
People can die here.

1419
01:36:06,678 --> 01:36:09,431
We need to know everything you know.
We need to know it now.

1420
01:36:09,514 --> 01:36:10,724
Okay.

1421
01:36:10,807 --> 01:36:14,561
But first, I'll take my car, my parents.
Maybe you should write that down.

1422
01:36:14,645 --> 01:36:19,358
Oh, and her juvie record.
That's got to be gone. Like, forever.

1423
01:36:20,984 --> 01:36:23,946
Come with me.
We'll talk about your car.

1424
01:36:24,029 --> 01:36:25,364
Thank you.

1425
01:36:26,573 --> 01:36:28,367
The man's an extortionist.

1426
01:36:30,285 --> 01:36:31,620
All right, here's the situation.

1427
01:36:31,703 --> 01:36:34,122
You've all had direct contact
with the NBEs.

1428
01:36:34,206 --> 01:36:35,332
NBEs?

1429
01:36:35,415 --> 01:36:39,044
Non-Biological Extraterrestrials.
Try and keep up with the acronyms.

1430
01:36:39,127 --> 01:36:42,798
What you're about to see
is totally classified.

1431
01:36:51,932 --> 01:36:53,809
Dear God. What is this?

1432
01:36:55,352 --> 01:36:58,647
We think when he made his approach
over the north pole,

1433
01:36:58,730 --> 01:37:02,150
our gravitational field screwed up
his telemetry.

1434
01:37:02,234 --> 01:37:06,279
He crashed in the ice,
probably a few thousand years ago.

1435
01:37:06,363 --> 01:37:09,658
We shipped him here to this facility
in 1934.

1436
01:37:09,741 --> 01:37:12,160
We call him NBE One.

1437
01:37:12,244 --> 01:37:14,621
Well, sir, I don't mean to correct you
on everything you think you know,

1438
01:37:14,705 --> 01:37:17,124
but, I mean, that's Megatron.

1439
01:37:18,375 --> 01:37:20,210
He's the leader of the Decepticons.

1440
01:37:20,293 --> 01:37:23,672
He's been in cryostasis since 1935.

1441
01:37:23,755 --> 01:37:27,217
Your great-great-grandfather made
one of the greatest discoveries

1442
01:37:27,300 --> 01:37:28,760
in the history of mankind.

1443
01:37:28,844 --> 01:37:31,805
Fact is, you're looking at
the source of the modern age,

1444
01:37:31,888 --> 01:37:38,729
the microchip, lasers, spaceflight, cars,
all reverse-engineered by studying him.

1445
01:37:38,812 --> 01:37:42,649
NBE One. That's what we call it.

1446
01:37:43,191 --> 01:37:45,861
And you didn't think the United States
military might need to know

1447
01:37:45,944 --> 01:37:48,321
that you're keeping a hostile alien robot
frozen in the basement?

1448
01:37:48,405 --> 01:37:52,409
Until these events, we had no
credible threat to national security.

1449
01:37:52,492 --> 01:37:54,411
Well, you got one now.

1450
01:37:55,287 --> 01:37:57,706
- So why Earth?
- It's the All Spark.

1451
01:37:57,789 --> 01:37:59,374
All Spark? What is that?

1452
01:37:59,458 --> 01:38:02,044
Well, yeah, they came here looking
for some sort of cube-looking thing.

1453
01:38:02,127 --> 01:38:06,882
Anyway, Mr. NBE One here, AKA
Megatron, that's what they call him,

1454
01:38:06,965 --> 01:38:09,426
who's pretty much the harbinger
of death, wants to use the Cube

1455
01:38:09,509 --> 01:38:12,637
to transform human technology
to take over the universe.

1456
01:38:12,721 --> 01:38:14,264
That's their plan.

1457
01:38:14,347 --> 01:38:16,808
- And you're sure about that?
- Yeah.

1458
01:38:19,102 --> 01:38:21,396
You guys know where it is, don't you?

1459
01:38:22,814 --> 01:38:23,982
Follow me.

1460
01:38:27,569 --> 01:38:30,113
You're about to see our crown jewel.

1461
01:38:38,997 --> 01:38:42,626
Carbon dating puts the Cube here
around 10,000 BC.

1462
01:38:43,502 --> 01:38:47,130
The first Seven didn't find it until 1913.

1463
01:38:47,964 --> 01:38:51,843
They knew it was alien because of
the matching hieroglyphics on the Cube

1464
01:38:51,927 --> 01:38:53,470
as well as NBE One.

1465
01:38:53,553 --> 01:38:56,139
President Hoover had the dam built
around it.

1466
01:38:56,223 --> 01:38:58,600
Four football fields thick of concrete.

1467
01:38:58,683 --> 01:39:02,062
A perfect way to hide its energy
from being detected by anyone

1468
01:39:02,145 --> 01:39:05,774
or any alien species on the outside.

1469
01:39:44,563 --> 01:39:48,400
Wait, back up. You said
the dam hides the Cube's energy.

1470
01:39:48,984 --> 01:39:51,528
- What kind exactly?
- Good question.

1471
01:39:56,116 --> 01:39:59,035
Please step inside.
They have to lock us in.

1472
01:40:04,916 --> 01:40:06,585
Oh, wow.

1473
01:40:06,668 --> 01:40:08,712
What's that? Freddy Krueger done
been up in here or something?

1474
01:40:08,795 --> 01:40:10,046
Oh, no, man.

1475
01:40:10,130 --> 01:40:14,634
Freddy Krueger have four blades, man.
That's only three. That's Wolverine!

1476
01:40:14,718 --> 01:40:17,679
- Right? That's Wolverine!
- That's very funny.

1477
01:40:19,181 --> 01:40:22,225
Anybody have any mechanical devices?
BlackBerry? Key alarm? Cell phone?

1478
01:40:22,309 --> 01:40:23,768
I got a phone.

1479
01:40:26,938 --> 01:40:29,566
Nokias are real nasty.

1480
01:40:29,649 --> 01:40:34,112
You've got to respect the Japanese.
They know the way of the samurai.

1481
01:40:34,905 --> 01:40:37,032
Nokia's from Finland.

1482
01:40:37,115 --> 01:40:41,745
Yes, but he's, you know, a little strange.
He's a little strange.

1483
01:40:44,456 --> 01:40:50,086
We're able to take the Cube radiation
and funnel it into that box.

1484
01:41:03,725 --> 01:41:07,062
- Mean little sucker, huh?
- That thing is freaky!

1485
01:41:07,145 --> 01:41:10,815
Kind of like the itty-bitty
Energizer Bunny from hell, huh?

1486
01:41:21,826 --> 01:41:23,703
He's breaking the box.

1487
01:41:41,680 --> 01:41:42,806
Go! Go! Go!

1488
01:41:42,889 --> 01:41:44,015
Move!

1489
01:41:52,524 --> 01:41:55,193
Gentlemen, they know the Cube is here.

1490
01:41:55,944 --> 01:41:57,279
Banachek. What's going on?

1491
01:41:57,362 --> 01:41:59,239
Well, the NBE One hangar
has lost power...

1492
01:41:59,322 --> 01:42:00,407
- What?
- ...<i>and the backup generator</i>

1493
01:42:00,490 --> 01:42:02,492
- <i>is just not gonna cut it.</i>
- Do you have an arms room?

1494
01:42:08,873 --> 01:42:10,625
Megatron! Megatron! Megatron!

1495
01:42:10,709 --> 01:42:12,127
I'll bring security to the...

1496
01:42:12,210 --> 01:42:14,796
Get everyone to
the NBE One chamber now!

1497
01:42:14,879 --> 01:42:16,464
- The lights are out!
- Move it! Move it!

1498
01:42:16,548 --> 01:42:17,966
Let's go!

1499
01:42:18,049 --> 01:42:19,843
They're popping our generators!

1500
01:42:31,813 --> 01:42:33,231
Megatron melting!

1501
01:42:33,815 --> 01:42:36,901
<i>16502. We're losing pressure.</i>

1502
01:42:36,985 --> 01:42:39,195
Stand by! Set!

1503
01:42:39,279 --> 01:42:41,364
<i>We're losing pressure!</i>

1504
01:42:41,448 --> 01:42:44,909
<i>The cryogenic system is failing!
We're losing NBE One!</i>

1505
01:42:49,622 --> 01:42:52,334
Forty millimetre sabot rounds
on that table!

1506
01:42:52,417 --> 01:42:56,463
That's good. Get all the ammo you got.
Everything you can carry. Bring it.

1507
01:43:01,968 --> 01:43:04,637
You got to take me to my car.
You have to take me to my car.

1508
01:43:04,721 --> 01:43:05,764
He's gonna know what to do
with the Cube.

1509
01:43:05,847 --> 01:43:07,807
- Your car? It's confiscated.
- Then unconfiscate it.

1510
01:43:07,891 --> 01:43:09,642
We do not know what will happen
if we let it near this thing!

1511
01:43:09,726 --> 01:43:11,019
- You don't know.
- Maybe you know, but I don't know.

1512
01:43:11,102 --> 01:43:12,479
You just wanna sit here and wait
and see what happens?

1513
01:43:12,562 --> 01:43:14,564
I have people's lives at stake here,
young man.

1514
01:43:14,647 --> 01:43:16,441
Take him to his car!

1515
01:43:18,109 --> 01:43:19,361
Drop it.

1516
01:43:21,112 --> 01:43:22,781
Whoa! Whoa! Whoa!

1517
01:43:24,032 --> 01:43:26,076
Drop your weapon, soldier.

1518
01:43:26,534 --> 01:43:28,286
There's an alien war going on
and you're gonna shoot me?

1519
01:43:28,370 --> 01:43:29,412
You know, we didn't ask to be here.

1520
01:43:29,496 --> 01:43:31,706
I'm ordering you under S-Seven
executive jurisdiction.

1521
01:43:31,790 --> 01:43:32,999
S-Seven don't exist.

1522
01:43:33,083 --> 01:43:34,876
Right. And we don't take orders
from people that don't exist.

1523
01:43:34,959 --> 01:43:38,254
- I'm gonna count to five. Okay.
- Well, I'm gonna count to three.

1524
01:43:40,799 --> 01:43:42,467
- Simmons?
- Yes, sir?

1525
01:43:42,550 --> 01:43:46,638
I'd do what he says. Losing's really
not an option for these guys.

1526
01:43:51,142 --> 01:43:53,103
All right. Okay.

1527
01:43:53,186 --> 01:43:57,732
Hey, you want to lay the fate of the
world on the kid's Camaro? That's cool.

1528
01:44:01,277 --> 01:44:02,570
No, no!

1529
01:44:03,488 --> 01:44:06,199
Stop! You got to stop! Stop! Stop! Stop!

1530
01:44:06,282 --> 01:44:09,869
No, no, stop, stop, stop!
Let him go! Let him go!

1531
01:44:11,037 --> 01:44:12,497
Are you okay?

1532
01:44:14,332 --> 01:44:16,459
They didn't hurt you, right?

1533
01:44:25,176 --> 01:44:29,013
Listen to me. The Cube is here
and the Decepticons are coming.

1534
01:44:31,349 --> 01:44:33,476
No, no, don't worry about them.
They're okay. Right?

1535
01:44:33,560 --> 01:44:35,812
They're not gonna hurt you.

1536
01:44:35,895 --> 01:44:39,441
Just back up a little bit.
He's friendly. He's fine.

1537
01:44:39,524 --> 01:44:42,819
Okay, come on. Put the guns down.
They're not gonna hurt you.

1538
01:44:42,902 --> 01:44:44,446
Here, come with me.
I'm gonna take you to the All Spark.

1539
01:45:06,468 --> 01:45:10,013
Okay, here we go. He doing something.
He doing something.

1540
01:45:30,074 --> 01:45:31,451
Oh, my God.

1541
01:45:36,247 --> 01:45:37,665
<i>Message from Starfleet, Captain.</i>

1542
01:45:37,749 --> 01:45:39,167
<i>Let's get to it.</i>

1543
01:45:39,250 --> 01:45:42,295
He's right. We stay here, we're screwed
with Megatron in the other hangar.

1544
01:45:42,378 --> 01:45:43,796
Mission City is 22 miles away.

1545
01:45:43,880 --> 01:45:45,173
We're gonna sneak that Cube
out of here

1546
01:45:45,256 --> 01:45:46,674
and we're gonna hide it somewhere
in the city.

1547
01:45:46,758 --> 01:45:47,759
Good! Right.

1548
01:45:47,842 --> 01:45:50,595
But we cannot make a stand
without the Air Force.

1549
01:45:50,678 --> 01:45:52,764
This place must have some kind
of radio link!

1550
01:45:52,847 --> 01:45:54,724
- Yes. Shortwave, CB.
- Right, yes.

1551
01:45:54,807 --> 01:45:57,435
Sir, you got to figure out some way
to get word out to them. Let's move!

1552
01:45:57,519 --> 01:45:58,978
In the alien archive, sir!

1553
01:45:59,062 --> 01:46:01,064
- The alien...
- There's an old Army radio console.

1554
01:46:01,147 --> 01:46:02,690
- Will it work?
- Anything's possible!

1555
01:46:02,774 --> 01:46:05,235
- Did you see that...
- All right, Sam, get it in the car!

1556
01:46:05,318 --> 01:46:07,111
Mr. Secretary! Get our birds in the air.

1557
01:46:07,195 --> 01:46:08,863
When we get to the city,
we're gonna find a radio,

1558
01:46:08,947 --> 01:46:10,907
and I'll have Epps vector them in, okay?

1559
01:46:10,990 --> 01:46:12,534
Affirmative!

1560
01:46:12,617 --> 01:46:16,496
<i>Warning! NBE One
cryo-containment failing.</i>

1561
01:46:17,455 --> 01:46:19,374
Check that backup system!

1562
01:46:19,457 --> 01:46:23,628
The cryo's failing! You got to bump up
the cryo! The cryo's failing!

1563
01:46:23,711 --> 01:46:25,213
Come on! Get out of here!

1564
01:46:25,296 --> 01:46:26,881
Heads up! Look out!

1565
01:46:27,840 --> 01:46:30,260
Set a perimeter around
the yellow vehicle!

1566
01:46:30,343 --> 01:46:33,805
- This way, this way, this way!
- Up there! Let's go!

1567
01:46:43,481 --> 01:46:46,609
I am Megatron!

1568
01:47:05,378 --> 01:47:06,796
- The Cube's okay?
- Yeah, it's fine.

1569
01:47:06,879 --> 01:47:07,922
Well, put the seat belt on.

1570
01:47:08,006 --> 01:47:09,173
Pour it on him!

1571
01:47:22,895 --> 01:47:24,939
I live to serve you, Lord Megatron.

1572
01:47:25,023 --> 01:47:27,442
Where is the Cube?

1573
01:47:27,525 --> 01:47:29,611
The humans have taken it.

1574
01:47:32,947 --> 01:47:36,868
You fail me yet again, Starscream.
Get them!

1575
01:47:37,243 --> 01:47:38,745
Come on, Mags!

1576
01:47:39,829 --> 01:47:41,372
Over here, sir!

1577
01:47:43,666 --> 01:47:45,752
Give me a minute. Give me a minute.

1578
01:47:45,835 --> 01:47:48,296
Come to me, Maxwell, come to me.
Plugged in there.

1579
01:47:50,173 --> 01:47:53,676
- We're hot! We're live!
- Where are the mikes?

1580
01:47:54,677 --> 01:47:55,678
Mikes?

1581
01:47:55,762 --> 01:47:57,055
This doesn't work without mikes,
Simmons.

1582
01:47:57,138 --> 01:47:58,723
No, no, no, no, no, no, no!

1583
01:47:58,806 --> 01:48:00,350
Let's find them.

1584
01:48:00,433 --> 01:48:01,934
Kid, get in the chair!
Just get in the chair, all right?

1585
01:48:02,018 --> 01:48:04,187
- Okay, I'll sit. I'll sit.
- They steal everything out of this place.

1586
01:48:04,270 --> 01:48:07,357
How do we get the signal out?
How do we call the Air Force?

1587
01:48:07,440 --> 01:48:08,775
- Glen?
- Huh?

1588
01:48:08,858 --> 01:48:12,362
Can you hotwire this computer to
transmit a tone through the radio?

1589
01:48:12,445 --> 01:48:13,488
What good is that?

1590
01:48:13,571 --> 01:48:15,990
Morse code! You can use this
to transmit it through that!

1591
01:48:16,074 --> 01:48:19,661
Okay, I'll do it! Turn it around.
Okay, let's see.

1592
01:48:19,744 --> 01:48:21,579
Simmons, I need a screwdriver!

1593
01:48:33,341 --> 01:48:34,926
There's Optimus.

1594
01:48:52,819 --> 01:48:54,320
Almost done.

1595
01:48:56,114 --> 01:48:58,074
What the hell was that?

1596
01:49:01,119 --> 01:49:02,829
Barricade the door!

1597
01:49:05,540 --> 01:49:07,917
- Get something.
- Watch out!

1598
01:49:08,000 --> 01:49:10,128
Six, five, four, six, three.

1599
01:49:14,799 --> 01:49:17,176
Here! Put some rounds in!

1600
01:49:20,012 --> 01:49:21,472
Master search.

1601
01:49:22,348 --> 01:49:24,392
I got it! We're transmitting!

1602
01:49:24,475 --> 01:49:25,601
Send exactly what I say!

1603
01:49:25,685 --> 01:49:29,856
Get out of the way! Get out of the way!
Burn, you little sucker! Burn!

1604
01:49:29,939 --> 01:49:33,985
"This is Defence Secretary Keller.
Get me NORTHCOM commander."

1605
01:49:34,068 --> 01:49:35,653
- Whoa!
- Whoa!

1606
01:49:37,321 --> 01:49:38,364
What was that?

1607
01:49:38,448 --> 01:49:41,325
Authenticate emergency action.
Blackbird 1195...

1608
01:49:43,453 --> 01:49:45,496
Sir, I have an authenticated
air strike order from Sec Def.

1609
01:50:10,354 --> 01:50:12,356
- No, no, no, no, no.
- What?

1610
01:50:12,440 --> 01:50:15,902
It's the same cop!
Block them, block them, block them.

1611
01:50:37,089 --> 01:50:38,132
Oh, my God.

1612
01:51:06,661 --> 01:51:08,037
Cool, Mom!

1613
01:51:33,896 --> 01:51:35,940
This is so not good.

1614
01:51:54,375 --> 01:51:56,294
He's behind the pillar!

1615
01:52:02,133 --> 01:52:05,261
- Shoot that mother...
- Maggie, cover fire!

1616
01:52:08,347 --> 01:52:10,725
It's the Air Force! They're responding!

1617
01:52:14,562 --> 01:52:16,564
Sucker, burn!

1618
01:52:22,320 --> 01:52:23,654
Oh, shit!

1619
01:52:23,988 --> 01:52:26,032
Yes! They're sending F-22s to the city!

1620
01:52:27,199 --> 01:52:29,285
<i>Raptors, let's scramble,
scramble, scramble.</i>

1621
01:52:30,453 --> 01:52:32,747
<i>Strike and Dark Starroll call.</i>

1622
01:52:35,041 --> 01:52:36,542
<i>Looking out the right side.</i>

1623
01:52:37,418 --> 01:52:39,629
<i>Push to Kill Box One Alpha...</i>

1624
01:52:47,178 --> 01:52:50,765
- Come on, let's go! Mount up!
- Move out! Move out! Go! Go!

1625
01:52:50,848 --> 01:52:53,059
Here, I got shortwave radios.

1626
01:52:53,559 --> 01:52:55,770
Wait. What am I supposed to
do with these?

1627
01:52:55,853 --> 01:52:58,189
Well, use them! It's all we got!

1628
01:52:58,564 --> 01:53:01,609
This is like RadioShack dinosaur radios
or something, man.

1629
01:53:01,692 --> 01:53:04,612
I'm only gonna get 20 or 30 miles
out of these things.

1630
01:53:04,695 --> 01:53:07,448
Are there any aircraft orbiting the city?

1631
01:53:08,032 --> 01:53:09,617
F-22 at 12:00.

1632
01:53:09,700 --> 01:53:12,453
All right, I want planes for air cover
and get Black Hawks on station

1633
01:53:12,536 --> 01:53:14,413
to extract that Cube. You got it?

1634
01:53:16,874 --> 01:53:19,335
Air Force has arrived! Pop smoke!

1635
01:53:19,585 --> 01:53:21,253
Raptor, Raptor, do you copy?

1636
01:53:22,505 --> 01:53:23,714
<i>We have you visual.</i>

1637
01:53:25,341 --> 01:53:26,676
<i>Green smoke is the mark.</i>

1638
01:53:26,759 --> 01:53:30,262
<i>Provide air cover and vector
Black Hawks for extraction.</i>

1639
01:53:34,892 --> 01:53:36,894
It's Starscream!

1640
01:53:37,311 --> 01:53:39,021
Please tell me you copy.

1641
01:53:39,313 --> 01:53:41,649
Back up! Take cover! Bumblebee!

1642
01:53:45,403 --> 01:53:47,405
No, no, no, no, no! Move!

1643
01:53:47,488 --> 01:53:50,658
- Back up! Back up!
- Retreat! Fall back!

1644
01:53:50,741 --> 01:53:52,034
Incoming!

1645
01:54:17,101 --> 01:54:18,894
Anybody hurt? Everyone okay?

1646
01:54:18,978 --> 01:54:20,479
Clear the area!

1647
01:54:26,277 --> 01:54:27,820
Oh, my God.

1648
01:54:28,654 --> 01:54:31,574
Bumblebee? No. Your legs!

1649
01:54:31,949 --> 01:54:33,325
Your legs.

1650
01:54:34,869 --> 01:54:38,539
Here. Here, back, back, back, back!
You all right?

1651
01:54:40,041 --> 01:54:42,501
Please get up. Bumblebee? Get up!

1652
01:54:44,045 --> 01:54:45,296
Ratchet!

1653
01:54:47,131 --> 01:54:48,591
- What the hell was that?
- What are you talking about?

1654
01:54:48,674 --> 01:54:50,634
What do you mean, what am
I talking about? They shot at us!

1655
01:54:50,718 --> 01:54:53,095
F-22 pilots would never fly
below buildings.

1656
01:54:53,179 --> 01:54:55,389
That's alien. That ain't friendly!

1657
01:54:55,473 --> 01:54:58,309
You got to get up. You're okay.
You're okay.

1658
01:54:59,518 --> 01:55:00,561
Come on!

1659
01:55:00,644 --> 01:55:02,813
<i>Army Black Hawk inbound
to your location. Over.</i>

1660
01:55:04,565 --> 01:55:06,734
Alpha 273 degrees, 10 miles.

1661
01:55:06,817 --> 01:55:09,153
November Victor, 1.2 clicks north.

1662
01:55:27,338 --> 01:55:28,839
Move out! Let's go!

1663
01:55:35,221 --> 01:55:36,972
Let's go! Move!

1664
01:55:43,521 --> 01:55:45,231
I'm not gonna leave you.

1665
01:56:24,311 --> 01:56:26,397
Come on, Decepticon punk!

1666
01:56:32,653 --> 01:56:34,238
Oh, my God!

1667
01:56:46,750 --> 01:56:48,711
Concentrate your fire!

1668
01:56:59,597 --> 01:57:00,806
Come on. Come on.

1669
01:57:03,350 --> 01:57:05,102
Megatron!

1670
01:57:09,773 --> 01:57:13,444
It's Megatron! Retreat! Move! Fall back!

1671
01:57:17,698 --> 01:57:19,325
Fall back!

1672
01:57:25,289 --> 01:57:27,541
Get our guys out of the way!
Get out of here! Go!

1673
01:57:27,625 --> 01:57:29,668
Get them out of the buggy! Move out!

1674
01:57:29,752 --> 01:57:32,046
We need air cover down here now!

1675
01:57:38,010 --> 01:57:39,470
Sam, help me with this.

1676
01:57:43,599 --> 01:57:47,937
- That all you got, Megatron?
- Come here, little cretin.

1677
01:57:48,020 --> 01:57:50,147
You want a piece of me?
You want a piece?

1678
01:57:50,231 --> 01:57:52,566
No! I want two!

1679
01:57:54,109 --> 01:57:55,527
What's going on?

1680
01:57:57,321 --> 01:57:59,990
Sir! That tank thing's getting back up.

1681
01:58:00,824 --> 01:58:03,118
Oh, these things just don't die.

1682
01:58:06,664 --> 01:58:08,165
Oh, we're so dead.

1683
01:58:08,249 --> 01:58:10,626
- Wrap it around the head.
- Sam!

1684
01:58:10,876 --> 01:58:11,919
Where's the Cube?

1685
01:58:12,002 --> 01:58:12,962
- Right there.
- Okay.

1686
01:58:13,045 --> 01:58:14,088
And take that and wrap it around

1687
01:58:14,171 --> 01:58:15,130
the base and then put it
around his neck.

1688
01:58:15,214 --> 01:58:17,925
- Okay?
- Epps, get those Black Hawks here!

1689
01:58:19,343 --> 01:58:20,844
That building.

1690
01:58:24,556 --> 01:58:26,392
- Okay.
- What?

1691
01:58:26,475 --> 01:58:29,436
All right, I can't leave my guys back
there, so here, take this flare.

1692
01:58:29,520 --> 01:58:31,814
Okay, there's a tall, white building
with statues on top.

1693
01:58:31,897 --> 01:58:34,108
- Go to the roof. Set the flare.
- No.

1694
01:58:34,191 --> 01:58:36,151
- Signal the chopper and set the flare.
- No, no. I can't do this!

1695
01:58:36,235 --> 01:58:40,656
Listen to me! You're a soldier now!
All right? I need you to take this Cube.

1696
01:58:40,739 --> 01:58:42,992
Get it into military hands
while we hold them off,

1697
01:58:43,075 --> 01:58:45,202
or a lot of people are gonna die.

1698
01:58:45,286 --> 01:58:46,787
- You got to go. You got to go.
- No, I'm not leaving.

1699
01:58:46,870 --> 01:58:48,080
- You need to go. Go.
- No, I'm not leaving

1700
01:58:48,163 --> 01:58:50,874
till I get Bumblebee out of here, okay?

1701
01:58:52,334 --> 01:58:53,419
Army Black Hawk requested.

1702
01:58:53,502 --> 01:58:56,046
Immediate evac for civilian boy
with precious cargo.

1703
01:58:56,130 --> 01:58:58,674
<i>Headed to rooftop marked by flare.</i>

1704
01:58:58,757 --> 01:59:01,885
- Sam, we will protect you.
- Okay.

1705
01:59:03,470 --> 01:59:06,849
- Epps, where are those planes?
- Sam!

1706
01:59:10,769 --> 01:59:14,940
No matter what happens,
I'm really glad I got in that car with you.

1707
01:59:18,152 --> 01:59:20,821
Sam! Get to the building! Move!

1708
01:59:20,904 --> 01:59:24,158
- Decepticons, attack!
- Hit it!

1709
01:59:26,869 --> 01:59:28,996
- Cover fire!
- Move to cover!

1710
01:59:35,419 --> 01:59:36,754
Watch out!

1711
01:59:42,301 --> 01:59:45,346
- Girl, get that tow truck out of here!
- I'm going! I'm going!

1712
01:59:45,429 --> 01:59:47,139
Get out of here now!

1713
02:00:14,958 --> 02:00:15,959
Megatron!

1714
02:00:16,251 --> 02:00:17,252
Prime.

1715
02:00:43,153 --> 02:00:45,239
Humans don't deserve to live.

1716
02:00:45,322 --> 02:00:48,033
They deserve to choose for themselves.

1717
02:00:48,450 --> 02:00:50,828
Then you will die with them!

1718
02:00:56,500 --> 02:00:58,919
Join them in extinction!

1719
02:01:18,105 --> 02:01:19,815
Keep moving, Sam!

1720
02:01:20,774 --> 02:01:22,192
Don't stop!

1721
02:01:38,167 --> 02:01:39,209
No!

1722
02:01:54,391 --> 02:01:56,518
Sam, get to the building!

1723
02:02:04,401 --> 02:02:06,570
Give me that Cube, boy!

1724
02:02:19,166 --> 02:02:21,293
Did that jerk just dent my car?

1725
02:02:42,606 --> 02:02:46,109
You're not gonna get me.
You're not gonna get me!

1726
02:02:51,406 --> 02:02:54,576
I smell you, boy!

1727
02:03:06,755 --> 02:03:07,965
Maggot!

1728
02:03:26,942 --> 02:03:28,569
Oh, no!

1729
02:03:53,093 --> 02:03:54,970
I'll drive! You shoot!

1730
02:04:15,866 --> 02:04:17,200
This isn't going well!

1731
02:04:17,284 --> 02:04:18,702
Shoot! Shoot!

1732
02:05:04,539 --> 02:05:05,791
Nice shot.

1733
02:05:05,874 --> 02:05:09,378
- That tank is definitely dead now.
- All right, let's go! We got business!

1734
02:05:19,805 --> 02:05:20,931
Hey!

1735
02:05:24,351 --> 02:05:27,813
Hey! I'm over here!

1736
02:05:40,117 --> 02:05:41,868
We've got the boy.

1737
02:05:46,456 --> 02:05:47,916
Watch out!

1738
02:05:48,250 --> 02:05:49,459
Missile!

1739
02:05:59,928 --> 02:06:01,388
Hang on, Sam!

1740
02:06:10,105 --> 02:06:11,481
No! No!

1741
02:06:17,154 --> 02:06:22,200
Is it fear or courage
that compels you, fleshling?

1742
02:06:35,714 --> 02:06:37,215
Where do I go?

1743
02:06:38,508 --> 02:06:42,512
Give me the All Spark
and you may live to be my pet.

1744
02:06:43,805 --> 02:06:45,474
Oh, no, no, no, no.

1745
02:06:49,603 --> 02:06:52,063
I'm never giving you this All Spark!

1746
02:06:52,189 --> 02:06:55,025
Oh, so unwise.

1747
02:07:06,912 --> 02:07:08,455
I got you, boy.

1748
02:07:10,207 --> 02:07:12,042
Hold on to the Cube!

1749
02:07:31,728 --> 02:07:34,606
- Oh, no. Oh, no!
- Disgusting.

1750
02:07:39,569 --> 02:07:40,654
Sam?

1751
02:07:44,908 --> 02:07:48,161
You risked your life to protect the Cube.

1752
02:07:48,870 --> 02:07:50,372
No sacrifice,

1753
02:07:51,706 --> 02:07:54,793
- no victory.
- If I cannot defeat Megatron,

1754
02:07:55,085 --> 02:07:57,629
you must push the Cube into my chest.

1755
02:07:58,004 --> 02:08:01,258
I will sacrifice myself to destroy it.

1756
02:08:01,675 --> 02:08:03,176
Get behind me.

1757
02:08:04,845 --> 02:08:07,430
It's you and me, Megatron.

1758
02:08:07,514 --> 02:08:10,475
No, it's just me, Prime.

1759
02:08:12,894 --> 02:08:18,066
At the end of this day,
one shall stand, one shall fall.

1760
02:08:23,446 --> 02:08:28,285
You still fight for the weak!
That is why you lose!

1761
02:08:47,429 --> 02:08:49,848
Fighter jets in 60 seconds.

1762
02:08:49,931 --> 02:08:52,392
We got friendlies mixed with bad guys.
Targets will be marked.

1763
02:08:52,475 --> 02:08:53,560
Hey.

1764
02:08:54,728 --> 02:08:56,938
Bring the rain. All right?

1765
02:08:57,314 --> 02:08:59,316
All right, let's kill these things.

1766
02:09:01,276 --> 02:09:02,861
- Move, move, move!
- Remember, aim low.

1767
02:09:02,944 --> 02:09:04,988
Armour's weak under the chest.

1768
02:09:14,998 --> 02:09:16,583
Target marked. Still waiting.

1769
02:09:16,666 --> 02:09:18,752
<i>Time on target, 20 seconds.</i>

1770
02:09:25,675 --> 02:09:27,802
F-22s, we're still waiting.

1771
02:09:33,016 --> 02:09:34,476
Move out!

1772
02:09:37,687 --> 02:09:38,939
Incoming!

1773
02:09:47,447 --> 02:09:49,574
<i>Weapons armed. Status green.</i>

1774
02:10:08,218 --> 02:10:10,053
Run! Move!

1775
02:10:17,560 --> 02:10:19,104
<i>Second wave's on approach.</i>

1776
02:10:22,565 --> 02:10:24,192
<i>What is that? Break off!</i>

1777
02:10:24,275 --> 02:10:26,778
<i>- Copy.
- It's either a massive amount of...</i>

1778
02:10:35,495 --> 02:10:37,706
<i>Two, get a lock! Pop that guy!</i>

1779
02:10:41,751 --> 02:10:43,712
<i>Stay on him. Keep him in your sights.</i>

1780
02:10:44,212 --> 02:10:45,547
Take him out!

1781
02:10:59,728 --> 02:11:01,104
Two's down!

1782
02:11:10,488 --> 02:11:12,449
I'll kill you!

1783
02:11:12,532 --> 02:11:15,285
Mine! All Spark!

1784
02:11:16,244 --> 02:11:19,122
Sam! Put the Cube in my chest! Now!

1785
02:11:19,789 --> 02:11:20,874
Sam!

1786
02:11:21,708 --> 02:11:22,959
No, Sam!

1787
02:11:48,693 --> 02:11:49,944
Hold up.

1788
02:11:52,989 --> 02:11:55,992
You left me no choice, brother.

1789
02:12:05,585 --> 02:12:08,505
Sam, I owe you my life.

1790
02:12:09,589 --> 02:12:11,341
We are in your debt.

1791
02:12:30,860 --> 02:12:33,279
Prime, we couldn't save him.

1792
02:12:34,114 --> 02:12:35,448
Jazz.

1793
02:12:38,618 --> 02:12:40,870
We lost a great comrade

1794
02:12:42,163 --> 02:12:44,040
but gained new ones.

1795
02:12:44,290 --> 02:12:46,626
Thank you, all of you.

1796
02:12:46,918 --> 02:12:49,337
You honour us with your bravery.

1797
02:12:50,338 --> 02:12:52,340
Permission to speak, sir?

1798
02:12:52,799 --> 02:12:55,677
Permission granted, old friend.

1799
02:12:55,760 --> 02:12:57,262
You speak now?

1800
02:12:58,179 --> 02:13:00,306
I wish to stay with the boy.

1801
02:13:01,141 --> 02:13:03,017
If that is his choice.

1802
02:13:07,897 --> 02:13:08,982
Yes.

1803
02:13:29,586 --> 02:13:34,382
Gentlemen, the President has ordered
Sector Seven be terminated

1804
02:13:34,883 --> 02:13:37,927
and the remains of the dead aliens
disposed of.

1805
02:13:38,553 --> 02:13:41,848
<i>The Laurentian Abyss is
seven miles below sea level,</i>

1806
02:13:41,931 --> 02:13:44,100
<i>deepest place on our planet.</i>

1807
02:13:44,267 --> 02:13:47,854
<i>The massive depth and pressure there,
coupled with subfreezing temperatures,</i>

1808
02:13:47,937 --> 02:13:50,148
<i>would crush and entomb them,</i>

1809
02:13:51,941 --> 02:13:53,693
<i>leaving no evidence.</i>

1810
02:14:00,283 --> 02:14:04,746
<i>With the All Spark gone,
we cannot return life to our planet.</i>

1811
02:14:06,456 --> 02:14:09,083
<i>And fate has yielded its reward,</i>

1812
02:14:10,585 --> 02:14:13,504
<i>a new world to call home.</i>

1813
02:14:19,761 --> 02:14:23,973
<i>We live among its people now,
hiding in plain sight,</i>

1814
02:14:24,098 --> 02:14:26,893
<i>but watching over them in secret,</i>

1815
02:14:27,101 --> 02:14:29,687
<i>waiting, protecting.</i>

1816
02:14:31,064 --> 02:14:34,150
<i>I have witnessed
their capacity for courage.</i>

1817
02:14:34,692 --> 02:14:37,737
<i>And though we are worlds apart,</i>

1818
02:14:37,820 --> 02:14:42,784
<i>like us, there's more to them
than meets the eye.</i>

1819
02:14:44,285 --> 02:14:46,829
<i>I am Optimus Prime</i>

1820
02:14:47,163 --> 02:14:50,583
<i>and I send this message
to any surviving Autobots</i>

1821
02:14:50,667 --> 02:14:53,670
<i>taking refuge among the stars.</i>

1822
02:14:54,671 --> 02:14:56,464
<i>We are here.</i>

1823
02:14:57,006 --> 02:14:59,050
<i>We are waiting.</i>

1824
02:15:18,361 --> 02:15:23,408
Can you shed any light on the recent,
so-called alien activity in the area?

1825
02:15:26,369 --> 02:15:31,916
Do you know what? I think that
if there was some sort of an alien

1826
02:15:32,500 --> 02:15:34,419
- infestation...
- Yeah.

1827
02:15:34,752 --> 02:15:37,213
They, the government,
would be the first to let you know.

1828
02:15:37,297 --> 02:15:39,007
The government would let us know.

1829
02:15:39,132 --> 02:15:40,758
- I mean, this is America.
- Yeah.

1830
02:15:40,842 --> 02:15:43,303
You know, that's how we know
we live in a free land,

1831
02:15:43,386 --> 02:15:45,013
because there's no secrets.

1832
02:15:45,096 --> 02:15:47,223
They'd say, "Hey! Duck and cover."

1833
02:15:57,233 --> 02:16:00,570
Your head is kind of a different size
than it is on television.

